//@version=6
// HALYARD + BREAK-THEN-VWAP (ORB + IB) - three setups, one script, one equity curve.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
//   Halyard is a 15-minute opening-range break that fires on the 15m CLOSE. Break-then-Pullback (ORB + IB) is a
//   pullback-limit engine that wants a fast chart. Run separately you cannot see their combined equity curve,
//   because a chart has one timeframe and Halyard would only be right on a 15m chart.
//   Here Halyard builds its own 15-minute bars out of whatever bars the chart is showing, so the WHOLE file can
//   be run on a 1-MINUTE chart and Halyard still trades exactly the 15m opens, highs, lows and closes it would
//   have traded on a 15m chart. Run this on 1m: ORB/IB get the resolution their limit fills need, Halyard is
//   unaffected by the chart timeframe, and the Strategy Tester shows the three of them together.
//
// >>> THE ENTRY: THE 09:30 ANCHORED VWAP <<<
//   This file is the fib-pullback engine with ONE rule swapped. ORB and IB used to rest their limit on a fib
//   retracement of their own range - the 25%/75% line for a shallow close, the 50% line otherwise, with a
//   second average-down unit always at the 50% line. THOSE LEVELS ARE GONE. Both setups now rest a single
//   limit at the SESSION VWAP ANCHORED TO THE 09:30 NY OPEN.
//
//   Three consequences follow, and they are the whole difference between this file and the fib one:
//     1. ONE UNIT, NOT TWO. The VWAP is a single price, so there is no second level to average down into. ORB
//        and IB are one entry each. The avg-down contract/risk inputs and the avg-down R/R box toggle are kept
//        in the dialog so old settings still load, but NOTHING READS THEM - their titles say so.
//     2. THE LIMIT MOVES. A fib level is fixed the moment the range closes; the VWAP re-prices on every bar.
//        The resting order is therefore RE-ISSUED EVERY BAR at the current VWAP (strategy.entry with the same
//        id amends the order rather than stacking a second one), so the fill lands wherever the VWAP actually
//        is when price comes back to it - not at a stale level price never returns to. The stop is still the
//        far range edge, so the entry-to-stop distance moves too, and a risk-$ contract count is recomputed
//        bar by bar until the fill.
//     3. THE ENTRY CAN BE INVALID. A fib retracement is always between the break and the stop by construction.
//        The VWAP is not: it can drift onto, or past, the far range edge, which would mean an entry at or
//        beyond its own stop - a zero- or negative-risk trade whose risk-sized contract count explodes. The
//        setup is therefore only armed while the VWAP sits at least `orbibMinStopFrac` of the range away from
//        the stop, on the correct side of it. Below that the limit is pulled and the day is simply not traded.
//
//   Everything else is untouched: the same ranges and clocks, the same low-first/high-first direction rule, the
//   same close-depth, min-range, weekday, double-break and daily-loss filters, the same seat precedence, the
//   same cutoffs and flattens, the same Halyard engine, the same probability study and the same webhook.
//
// >>> SELECTABLE TARGETS AND STOPS (ORB / IB) <<<
//   What used to be four hardcoded target strings and a stop welded to the far range edge is now the
//   "Targets & stops - ORB / IB" input group. Defaults reproduce the old behaviour exactly, so an untouched
//   copy of this file trades identically to the previous version.
//     TARGET, per setup AND per direction (four dropdowns): Range edge (the broken level, no extension),
//       Ext 10% / 30% / 50% (that far beyond it, as a fraction of the range), or HOD/LOD (the session high for
//       a long, low for a short, taken AS IT STANDS ON THE FILL BAR and frozen there - a target that kept
//       tracking the running high could never be reached, since price cannot exceed its own high).
//     STOP, per setup: 50%, 75% or 100% of the range, measured as a retracement from the edge that broke. For
//       a LONG, 100% is the range low, 75% is a quarter of the way up from it, 50% is the midpoint; mirrored
//       for a short. This is the convention the probability table's "75% line" already used.
//   ONE INTERACTION IS WORTH KNOWING. The stop choice feeds the entry filter: the setup is only armed while the
//   VWAP sits at least orbibMinStopFrac (10%) of the range clear of the stop. A 100% stop leaves the whole
//   range for the VWAP to sit in; a 50% stop leaves only the half nearest the breaking edge. Tightening the
//   stop therefore does not just cut the risk per trade, it also cuts how many days qualify at all - expect
//   noticeably fewer trades at 50%. Halyard is unaffected: it keeps its own Risk:Reward target and its own
//   stop modes, in its own input groups.
//
// THE 15-MINUTE ENGINE (Halyard), in short
//   Every chart bar is put in a 15-minute bucket (UTC-aligned, which is where TradingView's own 15m bars sit).
//   The LAST chart bar of a bucket closes that 15m bar, so on a 1m chart the 09:44 bar closes the 09:30-09:45
//   candle - with process_orders_on_close = true the entry fills at that bar's close, i.e. at the 15m close
//   price itself. A bucket that ends inside a data gap is caught up on the first bar of the next bucket.
//   REQUIREMENT: use a chart timeframe that divides into 15 - 1, 3, 5 or 15 minutes. On anything larger the
//   "15m" bar degrades to the chart bar and Halyard's levels stop matching a real 15m chart.
//   RUN THIS ON 1m. The VWAP entry needs fine bars even more than the fib one did: the limit is re-priced once
//   per chart bar, so the chart timeframe is the granularity at which the level tracks the VWAP.
//
// HOW THE THREE SETUPS SHARE ONE POSITION
//   Pine nets every order into ONE position: an opposite-side entry would REVERSE another setup's trade, not
//   hedge it. So the seat is taken by one setup at a time, in this order of precedence:
//     1. A live HALYARD trade holds the seat. ORB and IB limits are PULLED while it runs and re-issued the
//        moment it closes; if price trades through the VWAP during the hold, that setup is forfeited for the
//        day. (The fib file left the resting order in place here, which let a held-back limit fill behind an
//        open Halyard trade. A moving limit has to be re-issued every bar anyway, so pulling it is both the
//        cheaper and the correct reading of the seat rule.)
//     2. A live ORB trade holds the seat against IB (the original ORB/IB rule, unchanged).
//     3. Halyard SKIPS its break if an ORB or IB trade is live. Halyard is a market order at the 15m close -
//        it cannot rest and wait - and its break still consumes the day, exactly like any other rejected filter.
//   Each engine flattens only its OWN entries (strategy.close per entry id), so Halyard's 13:30/14:30 ET day
//   flat can never close an open ORB/IB trade and the 15:30 ET EOD flatten can never close a Halyard trade.
//   The daily max-loss circuit breaker is the one exception: it closes everything, because that is its job.
//
// RISK/REWARD BOXES: all three setups draw the SAME box - a green reward box from the entry to the target, a
//   red risk box from the entry to the stop, a coloured border per setup (orange ORB, teal IB, fuchsia
//   Halyard) and one label carrying contracts, $ risk, $ reward, the R multiple and the 1-contract numbers.
//   The ORB and IB boxes are RE-PRICED every bar while their limit is still unfilled, because their entry
//   level is moving with the VWAP, and freeze on the bar that fills.
//
// WHAT CHANGED vs THE TWO STANDALONE FILES
//   - One strategy() call, so ONE set of properties: commission $0.5/contract and 1 tick slippage (the ORB/IB
//     settings) now apply to Halyard too, which shipped with zero of both. Halyard's share of the curve will
//     therefore read slightly worse here than in its own backtest. Change it in Properties if you want parity.
//   - process_orders_on_close = true (Halyard needs the 15m close as its fill). ORB/IB exits are stops and
//     limits, which fill intrabar either way; their entry limits become live at the close of the bar that
//     prices them and can therefore first fill on the NEXT bar, and their EOD flatten moves from the next
//     bar's open to the flatten bar's close. The fib file's fill tracking assumed a limit could fill on the
//     same bar that priced it - harmless for a level fixed when the range closed, wrong for one that moves,
//     so this file tracks the price actually resting on the book instead (or_restPx / ib_restPx).
//   - initial_capital 150000 - enough to carry both engines. Neither engine compounds: ORB/IB size from fixed
//     dollar budgets or fixed contracts, Halyard from a fixed $ risk, so capital only affects the % figures.
strategy("Halyard + Break-then-VWAP (ORB + IB)", overlay = true, pyramiding = 6,
     max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500,
     initial_capital = 150000, margin_long = 0, margin_short = 0,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, process_orders_on_close = true,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 0.5, slippage = 1)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mode: strategy or indicator
// Pine decides strategy() vs indicator() when the script compiles, so an input cannot change the file's type.
// What this switch does is silence every ORDER. In Indicator mode the ranges, levels, the VWAP, the risk/reward
// boxes, probability table and break alerts all keep running on identical rules - the chart is byte for byte
// the same - while nothing is bought or sold. All three state machines (Halyard included) run in both modes,
// so the boxes you see as an indicator are exactly the trades the strategy would have taken.
gMode     = "Mode"
runMode   = input.string("Strategy - place orders", "Run as", options = ["Strategy - place orders", "Indicator - drawings & alerts only"], group = gMode,
     tooltip = "STRATEGY: the full engine - entries, exits, EOD flatten, daily-loss halt and the PickMyTrade webhook. INDICATOR: none of those, so no trades and an empty Strategy Tester, but every level, box, label, table and break alert still works.")
ordersOn  = runMode == "Strategy - place orders"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strategy toggles (isolate each for backtesting)
gStrat    = "Strategies (toggle to track each separately)"
runHAL    = input.bool(true, "Run HALYARD strategy (15m break, timeframe-independent)", group = gStrat, tooltip = "Turn OFF to backtest ORB/IB alone.")
runORB    = input.bool(true, "Run ORB strategy", group = gStrat, tooltip = "Turn OFF to backtest the IB strategy alone in the Strategy Tester.")
runIB     = input.bool(true, "Run IB strategy",  group = gStrat, tooltip = "Turn OFF to backtest the ORB strategy alone.")
orbCarry  = input.bool(false, "Carry an unfilled ORB past the IB (test idea)", group = gStrat,
     tooltip = "OFF: an ORB limit that has not filled by the time the IB forms is cancelled - the standard rule. ON: that limit keeps resting, and keeps tracking the VWAP, so a return to the VWAP that finally arrives after 10:30 still gets taken. It gives way the moment the IB breaks its own range and arms a setup, and otherwise expires at the ORB cutoff or the EOD flatten.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Trade-day filters (see which weekday hurts each)
gDayO     = "Trade days - ORB"
orbMon    = input.bool(true, "ORB Monday",    group = gDayO)
orbTue    = input.bool(true, "ORB Tuesday",   group = gDayO)
orbWed    = input.bool(true, "ORB Wednesday", group = gDayO)
orbThu    = input.bool(true, "ORB Thursday",  group = gDayO)
orbFri    = input.bool(true, "ORB Friday",    group = gDayO)
gDayI     = "Trade days - IB"
ibMon     = input.bool(true, "IB Monday",    group = gDayI)
ibTue     = input.bool(true, "IB Tuesday",   group = gDayI)
ibWed     = input.bool(true, "IB Wednesday", group = gDayI)
ibThu     = input.bool(true, "IB Thursday",  group = gDayI)
ibFri     = input.bool(true, "IB Friday",    group = gDayI)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Risk sizing (PER ENTRY) - ORB / IB
// TWO ways to size, one active at a time - tick the one you want; each is followed by its own inputs.
// The VWAP entry is a SINGLE unit per setup, so only the FIRST-entry values are read. The average-down inputs
// below them are kept so saved settings still load, and are marked UNUSED in their own titles.
// Halyard has its own sizing block further down - it is a different setup with a different stop.
gRisk       = "Risk sizing - ORB / IB"
mFixed      = input.bool(true,  "1) Fixed contract size", group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1 (default). Trade exactly the contract counts below - no risk maths at all. If both modes are ticked this one wins; if neither is ticked this one is used.")
orbQty1In   = input.float(2, "   ORB contracts",    minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1. Contracts on the ORB unit (the limit at the 09:30 anchored VWAP).")
orbQty2In   = input.float(2, "   ORB contracts - AVG-DOWN (UNUSED)", minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "UNUSED. The VWAP is a single price, so the ORB setup has no second level to average down into. Kept so saved settings still load; nothing reads it.")
ibQty1In    = input.float(1, "   IB contracts",     minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 1. Contracts on the IB unit.")
ibQty2In    = input.float(1, "   IB contracts - AVG-DOWN (UNUSED)",  minval = 1, step = 1, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "UNUSED. See the ORB avg-down note above.")
mDlr        = input.bool(false, "2) Risk $ per trade", group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 2. Ignore the contract counts: size the entry so its risk equals the dollar amount below. The stop distance decides the count - and because the VWAP entry MOVES while the stop stays on the far range edge, that distance is recomputed every bar until the fill, so the resting order's quantity moves with it. Untick mode 1 for this to take effect. If the amount cannot cover a single contract at that stop distance, the setup is skipped.")
orbRiskDlr1 = input.float(150, "   ORB $ risk",     minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "MODE 2. Dollars risked on the ORB entry, entry to stop, measured at the VWAP as it stands on the bar the order is priced.")
orbRiskDlr2 = input.float(150, "   ORB $ risk - AVG-DOWN (UNUSED)",  minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "UNUSED. See the ORB avg-down note above.")
ibRiskDlr1  = input.float(150, "   IB $ risk",      minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk)
ibRiskDlr2  = input.float(150, "   IB $ risk - AVG-DOWN (UNUSED)",   minval = 1, step = 25, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "UNUSED. See the ORB avg-down note above.")
maxDayLoss  = input.float(0, "Daily max loss $ (0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 25, group = gRisk,
     tooltip = "A flat dollar stop for the whole day, counted from the equity at the 09:30 session open and including open floating P&L. The moment the day is down this much, EVERY open trade - Halyard included - is closed at market, every resting order is cancelled and no new setup is taken until the next session; the block latches. NOTE it starts counting at 09:30 ET, so a Halyard trade taken overnight is only covered from the open onwards. 0 turns it off. Needs the strategy engine, so it does nothing in Indicator mode.")

// One mode only: fixed contracts wins if both are ticked, and is the fallback if neither is.
rmFixed    = mFixed or not mDlr
sizeByRisk = not rmFixed
modeTxt    = rmFixed ? "Sizing: fixed contracts" : "Sizing: risk $ per entry"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Halyard - Position sizing
gHPS          = "Halyard - Position sizing"
halUseRiskSz  = input.bool(true, "Use $ Risk Position Sizing", group = gHPS)
halRiskUSD    = input.float(535, "Risk Per Trade ($)", minval = 0, group = gHPS)
halQtyFixed   = input.int(1, "Contracts (If Risk Sizing Off)", minval = 1, group = gHPS)
halMaxQty     = input.int(1000, "Max Contracts", minval = 1, group = gHPS, tooltip = "Hard cap on the risk-sized quantity.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Halyard - Trade management
// Both R:R inputs are exposed, not just the first: the reverse one is UNREAD while the toggle is off but goes
// LIVE the moment it is ticked, and shipping a toggle that silently arms a hidden number is a trap.
gHTM          = "Halyard - Trade management"
halRR         = input.float(0.8, "Risk:Reward (First Trade)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.01, group = gHTM)
halRevOn      = input.bool(false, "Enable Reverse Trade", group = gHTM, tooltip = "Also sets the day's fill cap: 2 on, 1 off.")
halRevRR      = input.float(1.0, "Risk:Reward (Reverse Trade)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.01, group = gHTM, tooltip = "Only read while Enable Reverse Trade is on.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Halyard - Day filter
// One direction setting per weekday. "Off" is a day that never trades.
gHD           = "Halyard - Day filter"
halDayTip     = "Read on the SESSION's day, which ends 13:30 / 14:30 ET - not on the calendar day."
halMon        = input.string("Long", "Monday", options = ["Both", "Long", "Short", "Off"], group = gHD, tooltip = halDayTip)
halTue        = input.string("Both", "Tuesday", options = ["Both", "Long", "Short", "Off"], group = gHD)
halWed        = input.string("Both", "Wednesday", options = ["Both", "Long", "Short", "Off"], group = gHD)
halThu        = input.string("Both", "Thursday", options = ["Both", "Long", "Short", "Off"], group = gHD)
halFri        = input.string("Both", "Friday", options = ["Both", "Long", "Short", "Off"], group = gHD)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Halyard - Range filter
// A DAY gate on the range candle's own size, in POINTS. 0 = off on either side. BOTH SHIP AT 0, so this
// changes nothing until a value is set.
gHR           = "Halyard - Range filter"
halRngMin     = input.float(0, "Min ORB Range (pts, 0=off)", minval = 0, step = 0.25, group = gHR, tooltip = "Skip the day if the range is narrower than this.")
halRngMax     = input.float(0, "Max ORB Range (pts, 0=off)", minval = 0, step = 0.25, group = gHR, tooltip = "Skip the day if the range is wider than this.")

// Min above Max passes on NOTHING, and a strategy that silently stops trading reads as "no signals today"
// rather than as a typo. Fail loudly instead.
if halRngMax > 0 and halRngMin > halRngMax
    runtime.error("Halyard Range Filter: Min ORB Range is above Max ORB Range, so no day can ever pass. Fix one of them.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Filters (ORB / IB)
gFilt     = "Filters - ORB / IB"
noDbl     = input.bool(true, "Skip double-break days (both range sides break)", group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "If the side OPPOSITE the setup direction also breaks (long: price trades below the range low; short: above the range high), cancel the pending entry and take no trade that day.")
orbDepth  = input.float(75, "ORB bias: max close depth into the range (%)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 5, group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "How far the range may CLOSE into its own body and still count. Depth is measured from the level that will break: for a short that is the range low, for a long the range high. 50 is the classic rule. 100 accepts any close and leaves only the which-extreme-came-first test.")
ibDepth   = input.float(75, "IB bias: max close depth into the range (%)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 5, group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "Same measurement as the ORB depth filter, applied to the 1-hour initial-balance range.")
orbMinRngPct = input.float(0.40, "Min ORB range (% of price, 0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 0.05, group = gFilt,
     tooltip = "Skip ORB setups whose 15-min opening range is smaller than this % of price (range / range-low * 100). IB is NOT filtered. Set 0 to disable.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Targets & stops (ORB / IB)
// Both are measured against the setup's OWN range (its high, its low, and the distance between them), so they
// mean the same thing on any instrument and at any range size. Halyard is not here - it sizes its target off a
// Risk:Reward multiple and stops on its own 15m range edge, which is a different scheme; see its own groups.
gExit    = "Targets & stops - ORB / IB"
tpTip    = "VWAP 1/2/3 sigma targets that many standard deviations of the 09:30 anchored VWAP above it for a long, below it for a short - the natural target when the ENTRY is that same VWAP. It is measured on the bar the entry fills and frozen there. Range edge = the level that broke, i.e. no extension. Ext 10/30/50% = that far BEYOND the broken edge, as a fraction of the range. HOD/LOD = the session high (long) or low (short) AS IT STANDS ON THE FILL BAR, and it is frozen there - a target that kept tracking the running high could never be reached, since price cannot exceed its own high. Before the fill the box previews it against the high so far, so it moves until the entry fills and then stops."
orbTpLIn = input.string("Ext 10%", "ORB target - LONG",  options = ["Range edge", "Ext 10%", "Ext 30%", "Ext 50%", "HOD/LOD", "VWAP 1 sigma", "VWAP 2 sigma", "VWAP 3 sigma"], group = gExit, tooltip = tpTip)
orbTpSIn = input.string("Ext 30%", "ORB target - SHORT", options = ["Range edge", "Ext 10%", "Ext 30%", "Ext 50%", "HOD/LOD", "VWAP 1 sigma", "VWAP 2 sigma", "VWAP 3 sigma"], group = gExit)
ibTpLIn  = input.string("Ext 30%", "IB target - LONG",   options = ["Range edge", "Ext 10%", "Ext 30%", "Ext 50%", "HOD/LOD", "VWAP 1 sigma", "VWAP 2 sigma", "VWAP 3 sigma"], group = gExit)
ibTpSIn  = input.string("Ext 30%", "IB target - SHORT",  options = ["Range edge", "Ext 10%", "Ext 30%", "Ext 50%", "HOD/LOD", "VWAP 1 sigma", "VWAP 2 sigma", "VWAP 3 sigma"], group = gExit)
slTip    = "How far back INTO the range the stop sits, measured from the edge that broke - the same convention the probability table's '75% line' uses. For a LONG: 100% is the range low, 75% is a quarter of the way up from it, 50% is the midpoint. Mirrored for a short.\n\nNOTE this interacts with the VWAP entry: a tighter stop leaves less room between it and the entry, and the setup is only armed while the VWAP is at least 10% of the range clear of the stop (orbibMinStopFrac). A 50% stop therefore only trades days whose VWAP has stayed close to the breaking edge, and will take noticeably fewer trades than 100%."
orbSlIn  = input.string("100% of range (far edge)", "ORB stop", options = ["50% of range", "75% of range", "100% of range (far edge)"], group = gExit, tooltip = slTip)
ibSlIn   = input.string("100% of range (far edge)", "IB stop",  options = ["50% of range", "75% of range", "100% of range (far edge)"], group = gExit)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Automation (PickMyTrade webhook -> Tradovate)
grpA      = "Automation - PickMyTrade"
autoOn    = input.bool(false, "Enable webhook alerts", group = grpA,
     tooltip = "Create ONE alert with condition 'alert() function calls only' and paste PickMyTrade's webhook URL. Alerts fire on the NET position; the seat rules keep the three setups from ever being open at once, so each alert maps to a single setup. Silent in Indicator mode.")
pmtToken  = input.string("", "PickMyTrade token", group = grpA)
pmtAcct   = input.string("", "Tradovate account id", group = grpA)
pmtSym    = input.string("MNQ1!", "Broker symbol", group = grpA)
pmtType   = input.string("market", "Order type", options = ["market", "limit"], group = grpA)
pmtDebug  = input.bool(true, "Show the last webhook payload on the chart", group = grpA,
     tooltip = "Prints the exact JSON the script last transmitted, as a label on the most recent bar. TradingView gives you no way to see an alert() message after it has fired, so this is how you check that sl and tp really are leaving with a price on them. Turn it off once you are satisfied.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Break alerts (manual trading)
grpBA     = "Break alerts (manual)"
brkAlerts = input.bool(true, "Alert when a range breaks (Halyard / ORB / IB)", group = grpBA,
     tooltip = "Fires a notification the moment a range breaks, with the direction and the planned entry/stop/target so you can place the trade yourself. For ORB and IB the entry quoted is the anchored VWAP AS IT STANDS ON THE BREAK BAR - it will keep moving until the order fills. Create ONE alert on this strategy with condition 'alert() function calls only'.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Risk / Reward tool
grpRR     = "Risk / Reward tool"
showRR    = input.bool(true, "Show risk/reward box at the break", group = grpRR)
showRR2   = input.bool(true, "  ... second box for the avg-down unit (UNUSED)", group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "UNUSED. The VWAP entry is a single unit, so there is no average-down box to draw. Kept so saved settings still load; nothing reads it.")
showRRHal = input.bool(true, "  ... and a box for the Halyard trade", group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "Halyard's risk/reward box, drawn exactly like the ORB and IB ones: green reward box, red risk box, one label with contracts, $ risk, $ reward and the R multiple. Border is fuchsia so it is told apart from ORB orange and IB teal.")
showVwap  = input.bool(true, "Show the 09:30 anchored VWAP", group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "The line the ORB and IB limits ride. It is drawn for the whole 09:30-16:00 session, whether or not a setup is armed.")
showFibs  = input.bool(true, "Show fib retracement lines (25/50/75) - ORB / IB", group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "CONTEXT ONLY - these are no longer entries. The entry is the anchored VWAP. The 25/50/75 lines are kept because the probability table still measures what price does after reaching them.")
showInfo  = input.bool(true, "Show strategy rules panel", group = grpRR)
ptVal     = input.float(2.0, "$ per point per contract", group = grpRR, tooltip = "MNQ=2, NQ=20, MES=5, ES=50. Used for the ORB/IB boxes and sizing. Halyard's own box and sizing read the symbol's point value directly.")
keepBox   = input.int(0, "Keep R/R boxes for the last N setups (0 = all)", 0, 250, group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "0 keeps every past setup's boxes and fib lines. Pine caps a script at 500 boxes and 500 lines, and a setup now draws two boxes and three fib lines.")
keepLab   = input.int(3, "Keep R/R labels for the last N setups (0 = all)", 0, 250, group = grpRR,
     tooltip = "The boxes are cheap to look at; the text labels are what makes a chart unreadable when they stack up. This keeps the $ labels on the newest few setups only, while the boxes stay for the whole history. 0 keeps every label.")

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Historical probabilities (ORB / IB)
grpP      = "Historical probabilities"
hiLive    = input.bool(true, "Highlight the live setup in the table", group = grpP,
     tooltip = "Tints the table row you are currently in: the range-size row of the setup that is running, and the pullback row for the depth price has reached so far. A > marks the row that is live right now.")
showTable = input.bool(true, "Show probability table", group = grpP)
tblPos    = input.string("Bottom right", "Table position", options = ["Top right", "Bottom right", "Bottom left", "Top left"], group = grpP)
bMode     = input.string("Auto (equal thirds)", "Size buckets", options = ["Auto (equal thirds)", "Manual (%)"], group = grpP,
     tooltip = "Applies to the size-segmented rows only. Range is measured as % of price so buckets stay comparable as price drifts. Auto: split each strategy's own range-% distribution into three equal-count buckets (S/M/L). Manual: use the fixed % thresholds below.")
orbB1     = input.float(0.25, "Manual ORB small/med split (%)", step = 0.05, group = grpP, tooltip = "Used only in Manual mode.")
orbB2     = input.float(0.40, "Manual ORB med/large split (%)", step = 0.05, group = grpP)
ibB1      = input.float(0.50, "Manual IB small/med split (%)",  step = 0.05, group = grpP)
ibB2      = input.float(0.80, "Manual IB med/large split (%)",  step = 0.05, group = grpP)
pbSplit   = input.bool(false, "Split the pullback rows by size too", group = grpP,
     tooltip = "OFF (default): one 'after 25% PB' and one 'after 50% PB' row per strategy, pooled across range sizes. ON: those rows are repeated per S/M/L bucket.")
autoMode  = bMode == "Auto (equal thirds)"

// ================================================================ HARDCODED CONFIG (edit values here)
// ---- shared session clock ----
tz      = "America/New_York"
sess    = "0930-1600"
orbSess = "0930-0945"
ibSess  = "0930-1030"
flatH   = 15
flatM   = 30
// ---- the 09:30 anchored VWAP (the ORB/IB entry level) ----
// Accumulated on the CHART's bars over the same 09:30-1600 session the rest of the file uses, and re-anchored
// every day at the open. hlc3 is the usual VWAP source and is what the standalone anchored-VWAP indicator in
// this repo uses, so the level here and the level there are the same number.
vwapSrc = hlc3
// The VWAP entry MOVES while the stop stays pinned to the far range edge, so the entry-to-stop distance is not
// guaranteed the way a fib retracement's was. This is the floor on that distance, as a FRACTION OF THE RANGE:
// below it the setup is not armed. It does two jobs - it refuses an entry that has drifted onto or past its own
// stop (a zero- or negative-risk trade), and it stops the risk-$ sizer dividing by a near-zero stop distance
// and returning an enormous contract count. For scale, the fib entries this replaced sat 25% and 50% of the
// range away from the stop, so 0.10 is a loose floor that rarely binds.
orbibMinStopFrac = 0.10
// ---- ORB settings ----
orbLong   = true
orbShort  = true
orbBreak  = "Close beyond"
orbAvg    = true              // UNREAD: the VWAP entry is a single unit, there is no average-down level
orbTpL    = orbTpLIn          // target per direction   (Targets & stops group)
orbTpS    = orbTpSIn
orbSl     = orbSlIn           // stop as a % of the range (Targets & stops group)
orbBE     = false
orbQty1   = orbQty1In         // contracts on the ORB entry              (Risk sizing group)
orbQty2   = orbQty2In         // UNREAD: no average-down unit
orbCutH   = 15
orbCutM   = 0
// ---- IB settings ----
ibLong    = true
ibShort   = true
ibBreak   = "Wick (touch)"
ibAvg     = true              // UNREAD: see orbAvg
ibTpL     = ibTpLIn           // target per direction   (Targets & stops group)
ibTpS     = ibTpSIn
ibSl      = ibSlIn            // stop as a % of the range (Targets & stops group)
ibBE      = false
ibQty1    = ibQty1In          // contracts on the IB entry               (Risk sizing group)
ibQty2    = ibQty2In          // UNREAD: no average-down unit
ibCutH    = 14
ibCutM    = 0
// ---- HALYARD settings ----
// Values marked UNREAD belong to a mode that is not selected - they are kept so the mode ternaries still
// compile, and a constant condition folds anyway.
// NOTE WHICH VALUES ARE LIVE: halTpType is Risk:Reward, so the Risk:Reward inputs above ARE read and
// halTpTicks / halAtrTpMult are not.
halDirection  = "Both"        // blanket override on top of the per-day grid
halSlType     = "ORB Edge + Buffer"
halSlBuf      = 0.0           // ZERO -> the stop sits exactly ON the opposite range edge
halSlTicks    = 340           // UNREAD under ORB Edge + Buffer
halAtrSlMult  = 3.8           // UNREAD under ORB Edge + Buffer
// UNREAD under ORB Edge + Buffer. Set halSlType = "Breakout Candle" to arm the fourth mode: the stop goes
// beyond the breakout candle instead of the far range edge, and halSlBuf is then measured past THAT extreme.
// 1 = the breakout candle alone; 2 or 3 also take in the 1-2 FIFTEEN-MINUTE candles before it (the window is
// built from the engine's own 15m bars, so it does not change with the chart timeframe), and since the level
// is the lowest low / highest high of that window, raising it can only widen the stop, never tighten it.
halSlBars     = 1
halTpType     = "Risk:Reward"
halTpTicks    = 90            // UNREAD under Risk:Reward
halAtrTpMult  = 5.0           // UNREAD under Risk:Reward
halAtrLen     = 32            // UNREAD: no ATR mode is picked
halMaxBars    = 0             // 0 = TIME STOP OFF. Counted in 15m bars. Only TP, SL and the day flat close a trade
// OFF, so there are no entry filters at all: the break, the weekday grid and the direction are the whole entry
// condition. Set true to arm the trend filter (shorts only).
halUseTrend   = false
halTrendEma   = 190
// Visual defaults. The breakout TRIANGLE marks the 15m bar that BREAKS the range, not the range candle itself.
halShowMarker = true
halUpCol      = color.new(color.green, 30)
halDnCol      = color.new(color.red, 30)
halSigCol     = color.new(color.fuchsia, 0)   // the Halyard R/R box border, vs ORB orange and IB teal

// The day's fill cap is DERIVED from the reversal switch (2 on, 1 off) rather than being a second,
// disagreeable input.
halMaxTrades = halRevOn ? 2 : 1

// ================================================================ Shared tracking (RTH session, ORB/IB clock)
inSess     = not na(time(timeframe.period, sess, tz))
newSession = inSess and not inSess[1]
var float dHigh = na
var float dLow  = na
if newSession
    dHigh := high
    dLow  := low
else if inSess
    dHigh := math.max(dHigh, high)
    dLow  := math.min(dLow, low)
tod     = hour(time, tz) * 60 + minute(time, tz)
flatten = tod >= (flatH*60 + flatM)

// ---- THE ENTRY LEVEL: session VWAP anchored to the 09:30 open ----
// Re-anchored on the first bar of the RTH session and accumulated only inside it, so each day is its own clean
// anchored VWAP and nothing leaks across the overnight. This is the level BOTH pullback setups now rest their
// limit on, in place of the 25%/50% fib retracements of their own range.
// It is na outside 09:30-16:00, which is exactly what the setups want: no VWAP, no entry.
var float vwPV  = 0.0   // sum(price * vol)
var float vwV   = 0.0   // sum(vol)
var float vwP2V = 0.0   // sum(price^2 * vol) - one power up, for the standard deviation
if newSession
    vwPV  := 0.0
    vwV   := 0.0
    vwP2V := 0.0
if inSess
    vwVol = nz(volume, 1.0)                   // fall back to 1 if the symbol has no volume
    vwPV  += vwapSrc * vwVol
    vwV   += vwVol
    vwP2V += vwapSrc * vwapSrc * vwVol
avwap = inSess and vwV > 0 ? vwPV / vwV : na
// The anchored VWAP's OWN standard deviation - the unit the sigma targets are measured in, and the natural
// one to use here because the ENTRY is that same VWAP. variance = E[p^2] - E[p]^2, floored at zero because
// floating point can push a barely-moving series a hair negative and sqrt would hand back na.
avwapVar = inSess and vwV > 0 ? math.max(vwP2V / vwV - avwap * avwap, 0) : na
avwapDev = na(avwapVar) ? na : math.sqrt(avwapVar)

// ---- daily loss limit: a flat $ stop for the whole session, floating P&L included ----
var float dayStartEq = na
var bool  dayHalt    = false
if newSession
    dayStartEq := strategy.equity
    dayHalt    := false
dayPnL = strategy.equity - dayStartEq                 // today's P&L, realised + open
if maxDayLoss > 0 and dayPnL <= -maxDayLoss
    dayHalt := true                                   // latched: the day stays shut once it trips

// day-of-week gates (per strategy) - ORB/IB read the calendar day, Halyard its own shifted session day
dow      = dayofweek(time, tz)
orbDayOK = (dow == dayofweek.monday and orbMon) or (dow == dayofweek.tuesday and orbTue) or (dow == dayofweek.wednesday and orbWed) or (dow == dayofweek.thursday and orbThu) or (dow == dayofweek.friday and orbFri)
ibDayOK  = (dow == dayofweek.monday and ibMon)  or (dow == dayofweek.tuesday and ibTue)  or (dow == dayofweek.wednesday and ibWed)  or (dow == dayofweek.thursday and ibThu)  or (dow == dayofweek.friday and ibFri)

or_inR   = not na(time(timeframe.period, orbSess, tz))
or_rDone = not or_inR and or_inR[1]
ib_inR   = not na(time(timeframe.period, ibSess, tz))
ib_rDone = not ib_inR and ib_inR[1]
var bool ibFormed = false
if newSession
    ibFormed := false
if ib_rDone
    ibFormed := true

// position sizer for ORB/IB: contracts for a $ budget at a given stop distance (points).
// round: fractional <= .5 -> down, > .5 -> up. A budget too small for a single contract returns 0, and the
// ">= 1" guards on the entries below simply skip that setup.
f_size(float budget, float ptDist) =>
    perC = ptDist * ptVal
    raw  = perC > 0 ? budget / perC : 0.0
    fr   = raw - math.floor(raw)
    fr > 0.5 ? math.ceil(raw) : math.floor(raw)

// TP resolver (ORB/IB)
// vw/dev carry the anchored VWAP and its standard deviation, so a sigma target can be resolved. They are read
// on the bar the entry fills and the answer is frozen there - a target that kept tracking would wander
// (sigma) or could never be reached at all (HOD, which price cannot exceed).
f_tp(int d, float rH, float rL, float rg, float dHi, float dLo, float vw, float dev, string tpL, string tpS) =>
    sg = nz(dev, 0.0)
    d == 1 ? (tpL == "HOD/LOD" ? dHi : tpL == "VWAP 1 sigma" ? vw + sg : tpL == "VWAP 2 sigma" ? vw + 2*sg : tpL == "VWAP 3 sigma" ? vw + 3*sg : tpL == "Ext 10%" ? rH + 0.10*rg : tpL == "Ext 30%" ? rH + 0.30*rg : tpL == "Ext 50%" ? rH + 0.50*rg : rH) : (tpS == "HOD/LOD" ? dLo : tpS == "VWAP 1 sigma" ? vw - sg : tpS == "VWAP 2 sigma" ? vw - 2*sg : tpS == "VWAP 3 sigma" ? vw - 3*sg : tpS == "Ext 10%" ? rL - 0.10*rg : tpS == "Ext 30%" ? rL - 0.30*rg : tpS == "Ext 50%" ? rL - 0.50*rg : rL)

// A target has to sit BEYOND the entry or the trade is nonsense, and with a free choice of target that is no
// longer guaranteed: a sigma band on a morning with almost no dispersion collapses onto the VWAP - which is
// the entry here - and a HOD/LOD target can already be behind an entry that filled on a spike. Anything not
// clear of the entry falls back to a 1R target, the stop distance mirrored, which is always a real level.
f_tpGuard(int d, float tp, float ent, float stp) =>
    ok = d == 1 ? tp > ent + syminfo.mintick : tp < ent - syminfo.mintick
    ok ? tp : (d == 1 ? ent + (ent - stp) : ent - (stp - ent))

// STOP resolver (ORB/IB): the stop as a RETRACEMENT of the range, measured from the edge that broke. This is
// the same convention the probability table's "75% line" uses, so the two agree by construction.
//   LONG  (broke the high): 100% -> the range low, 75% -> a quarter of the way up from it, 50% -> the midpoint.
//   SHORT (broke the low) : mirrored off the range high.
// Anything other than the two tighter strings falls through to 100%, so the far edge stays the default.
f_sl(int d, float rH, float rL, float rg, string mode) =>
    f = mode == "50% of range" ? 0.50 : mode == "75% of range" ? 0.75 : 1.00
    d == 1 ? rH - f * rg : rL + f * rg

// The seat: an ORB or IB position that is open right now. Declared HERE, filled in at the bottom of the ORB/IB
// engines, and read by Halyard above them - so Halyard sees the value as of the previous chart bar. On a 1m
// chart that is a one-minute lag on a gate that only matters when a fill and a 15m close land on the same bar.
var bool orbibLive = false

// ================================================================ HALYARD ENGINE  (UNCHANGED)
// Single-candle opening-range breakout with an optional loser-reversal, on 15-MINUTE candles that this engine
// builds itself - so the chart can be 1m, 3m, 5m or 15m and the levels, the break and the fills are identical.
//
// The range is one 15-minute candle. The first 15m bar that CLOSES beyond it takes the day's trade and consumes
// the day whichever side it fired on - there is no second attempt if the filters reject it. Stop sits on the
// opposite edge of the range, target is a multiple of that distance. Flat before the session rolls; nothing is
// ever carried overnight.
//
// Halyard is a market order at the 15m close and never rests, so the VWAP change does not touch it at all.
//
// The clock is HARDCODED to New York and the chart's own timezone setting moves nothing: every clock read
// passes `tz` explicitly. THE CONVERSION IS NOT A FIXED HOUR, which is the whole subtlety. The range candle is
// anchored to 10:30 Asia/Kolkata = 05:00 UTC every day of the year, because India has no DST and the US does.
// On the New York clock that is 00:00 under EST and 01:00 under EDT, so the ET hour has to FOLLOW the US
// changeover or it sits on the wrong bars for half the year. Both seasonal values are derived per bar.

// ET's UTC offset in minutes on bar `t`: 300 under EST, 240 under EDT. Read off the tape rather than assumed,
// because the entire point is that it moves. The `+ 1440 % 1440` is there because New York and UTC are usually
// on different calendar days, which sends the raw difference negative.
f_halEtOffset(t) =>
    etM = hour(t, tz) * 60 + minute(t, tz)
    (hour(t, "Etc/UTC") * 60 + minute(t, "Etc/UTC") - etM + 1440) % 1440

// 10:30 Asia/Kolkata written on the New York clock: 00:00 EST / 01:00 EDT.
f_halOrbStartMin(t) => f_halEtOffset(t) == 240 ? 60 : 0

// 00:00 Asia/Kolkata - the boundary the Halyard trading day rolls on - written on the same clock: 13:30 EST /
// 14:30 EDT. It resets the day's state, picks the day-of-week and force-flattens.
f_halSessionEndMin(t) => f_halEtOffset(t) == 240 ? 870 : 810

// The instant this bar's session ENDS, on the New York clock. Shifting a bar forward to its own boundary makes
// the session's date and weekday simply the ET date and weekday of the shifted instant - no wrap-around
// arithmetic anywhere, and the key and the day filter cannot drift apart because they read the same shift.
// Bumping a YYYYMMDD key by 1 instead LOOKS equivalent and is not: 20260531 + 1 is not 20260601, so every month
// boundary would split one session into two, resetting the day's state and force-flattening mid-session.
f_halSessionShift(t) => t + (1440 - f_halSessionEndMin(t)) * 60000

f_halSessionKey(t) =>
    s = f_halSessionShift(t)
    year(s, tz) * 10000 + month(s, tz) * 100 + dayofmonth(s, tz)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the 15-minute bar builder
// Buckets are aligned to the epoch, i.e. to :00/:15/:30/:45 UTC, which is exactly where TradingView's own 15m
// bars sit for these instruments (the CME reopen at 18:00 ET is on a 15-minute boundary in UTC too).
halTfMs  = 15 * 60 * 1000
chartMs  = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) * 1000
halBkt   = math.floor(time / halTfMs)

var int   halAggBkt  = na
var float halAggH    = na
var float halAggL    = na
var float halAggC    = na
var int   halAggT    = na
var bool  halBktDone = false

// set on the chart bar that CLOSES a 15-minute candle, together with that candle's H/L/C and open time
halNewBar = false
float hal15H = na
float hal15L = na
float hal15C = na
int   hal15T = na

// (1) CATCH-UP. A bucket whose last bar never arrived (a data gap, a halt, a session end) is closed here, on
//     the first bar of the next bucket, out of the aggregate as it stood. The aggregate still holds the
//     previous bar's values because it is rolled in step 2, below this.
if not na(halAggBkt) and halBkt != halAggBkt and not halBktDone
    halNewBar := true
    hal15H := halAggH
    hal15L := halAggL
    hal15C := halAggC
    hal15T := halAggT
// (2) ROLL the aggregate: start a new one on a new bucket, otherwise extend it.
if na(halAggBkt) or halBkt != halAggBkt
    halAggBkt  := halBkt
    halAggH    := high
    halAggL    := low
    halAggT    := time
    halBktDone := false
else
    halAggH := math.max(halAggH, high)
    halAggL := math.min(halAggL, low)
halAggC := close
// (3) PROJECTED CLOSE - the normal path. This chart bar is the last one of its bucket when the NEXT bar's time
//     falls in a different bucket, so the 15m candle closes here, at this bar's close. barstate.isconfirmed
//     keeps a forming bar from firing the break early.
if not halBktDone and barstate.isconfirmed and math.floor((time + chartMs) / halTfMs) != halBkt
    halBktDone := true
    halNewBar  := true
    hal15H := halAggH
    hal15L := halAggL
    hal15C := halAggC
    hal15T := halAggT

// the previous two CLOSED 15m candles, kept for the (unread) Breakout Candle stop mode; shifted at the very
// end of this engine so that during the entry logic they are still the bars BEFORE the breakout candle.
var float hal15L1 = na
var float hal15L2 = na
var float hal15H1 = na
var float hal15H2 = na

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- daily state
// Reset once per session, on the 13:30 / 14:30 ET boundary - NOT on ET midnight.
halSessKey = f_halSessionKey(time)
halNewDay  = nz(ta.change(halSessKey), 0) != 0

var float halRH   = na       // the range candle's high / low / open time
var float halRL   = na
var int   halRT   = na
var bool  halBroke = false   // the day's first break latches here and consumes the day whichever side it fired on
// State machine (per day):
// 0 = no trade yet (wait for first breakout) | 1 = first trade running | 2 = first trade stopped out (wait for
// an opposite-side 15m close beyond the range) | 3 = done for the day (first trade hit TP, or reversal taken)
var int   halState  = 0
var int   halFirstDir = 0
var int   halTrades = 0
// the live (simulated AND ordered) trade
var int   halTrDir  = 0      // 0 flat, 1 long, -1 short
var float halEnt    = na
var float halStp    = na
var float halTgt    = na
var float halQty    = na
var int   halEntBar = na
var int   halBars15 = 0      // 15m candles elapsed since the entry, for the (off by default) time stop

if halNewDay
    halRH := na
    halRL := na
    halRT := na
    halBroke := false
    halState := 0
    halFirstDir := 0
    halTrades := 0

// When a 15m candle closes AND it is the range candle, store its high/low as the day's levels.
halIsRangeBar = halNewBar and (hour(hal15T, tz) * 60 + minute(hal15T, tz)) == f_halOrbStartMin(hal15T)
if halIsRangeBar
    halRH := hal15H
    halRL := hal15L
    halRT := hal15T
    halBroke := false

halLevels = not na(halRH) and not na(halRL)
halRange  = halRH - halRL

// RANGE is a DAY gate: it gates the BREAKOUT LATCH, not the entry. That distinction is the whole behaviour - a
// day the range rejects is skipped ENTIRELY (no trade, no reversal, no triangle) and is NOT consumed, because
// halBroke can only latch on a day allowed to break out in the first place. Knowable at the bars it gates: the
// range is fixed when the range candle closes, which is before anything can trade that day.
halRangeOK = not na(halRange) and (halRngMin <= 0 or halRange >= halRngMin) and (halRngMax <= 0 or halRange <= halRngMax)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- indicators (only read by unselected modes)
// Taken from the 15-MINUTE series so they do not change with the chart timeframe. request.security publishes a
// value on the first chart bar of the next 15m period, and the engine acts on the LAST bar of the current one,
// so both are the value through the candle BEFORE the breakout candle. Both are off in the shipped config.
halAtrVal = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "15", ta.atr(halAtrLen), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
halEmaVal = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "15", ta.ema(close, halTrendEma), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- stop / target / size
// The Breakout Candle window, over the engine's own 15m candles. Only meaningful on a bar where a 15m candle
// closed; the stop helpers are only ever called on such a bar.
halWinLow  = halSlBars >= 3 ? math.min(hal15L, math.min(nz(hal15L1, hal15L), nz(hal15L2, hal15L))) : halSlBars == 2 ? math.min(hal15L, nz(hal15L1, hal15L)) : hal15L
halWinHigh = halSlBars >= 3 ? math.max(hal15H, math.max(nz(hal15H1, hal15H), nz(hal15H2, hal15H))) : halSlBars == 2 ? math.max(hal15H, nz(hal15H1, hal15H)) : hal15H
// Floored at one tick. halSlBuf ships at 0.0, and a breakout candle that closes on its own low puts the raw
// level exactly ON the entry reference the sizer divides by, so the risk per contract would be zero and the
// size would slam into the cap. The floor is what stops that.
// NOTE the unit: halSlBuf is POINTS, not ticks. On MNQ/NQ one tick is 0.25 points.
halCandleBuf = math.max(halSlBuf, syminfo.mintick)

f_halLongStop(entryPx) =>
    halSlType == "ORB Edge + Buffer" ? halRL - halSlBuf : halSlType == "Breakout Candle" ? halWinLow - halCandleBuf : halSlType == "Fixed Ticks" ? entryPx - halSlTicks * syminfo.mintick : entryPx - halAtrVal * halAtrSlMult

f_halShortStop(entryPx) =>
    halSlType == "ORB Edge + Buffer" ? halRH + halSlBuf : halSlType == "Breakout Candle" ? halWinHigh + halCandleBuf : halSlType == "Fixed Ticks" ? entryPx + halSlTicks * syminfo.mintick : entryPx + halAtrVal * halAtrSlMult

// rr is only reached in Risk:Reward mode - under ATR / Fixed Ticks the first trade and the reversal get the
// SAME distance.
f_halLongTP(entryPx, stopPx, rr) =>
    halTpType == "Risk:Reward" ? entryPx + (entryPx - stopPx) * rr : halTpType == "Fixed Ticks" ? entryPx + halTpTicks * syminfo.mintick : entryPx + halAtrVal * halAtrTpMult

f_halShortTP(entryPx, stopPx, rr) =>
    halTpType == "Risk:Reward" ? entryPx - (stopPx - entryPx) * rr : halTpType == "Fixed Ticks" ? entryPx - halTpTicks * syminfo.mintick : entryPx - halAtrVal * halAtrTpMult

// Quantity is auto-calculated from: risk$ / (abs(entry - stop) * point value of the symbol)
f_halQty(_entry, _sl) =>
    riskPerContract = math.abs(_entry - _sl) * syminfo.pointvalue
    q = halUseRiskSz ? math.max(math.floor(halRiskUSD / (riskPerContract > 0 ? riskPerContract : syminfo.mintick * syminfo.pointvalue)), 1) : halQtyFixed
    math.min(q, halMaxQty)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- day / direction grid
// The SESSION's day-of-week, not the bar's: a bar past the 13:30 / 14:30 ET boundary already belongs to
// tomorrow's session. Read off the same shifted instant as the session key, so the two agree by construction.
halDow  = dayofweek(f_halSessionShift(time), tz)
// Saturday and Sunday fall through to "Off" - nothing here has to special-case the weekend.
halMode = halDow == dayofweek.monday ? halMon : halDow == dayofweek.tuesday ? halTue : halDow == dayofweek.wednesday ? halWed : halDow == dayofweek.thursday ? halThu : halDow == dayofweek.friday ? halFri : "Off"
halDayOK = halMode != "Off"
// The per-day setting ANDs into the global direction rather than replacing it, so the global still works as a
// blanket override on top of the per-day grid.
halLongOK  = (halDirection == "Both" or halDirection == "Long")  and (halMode == "Both" or halMode == "Long")
halShortOK = (halDirection == "Both" or halDirection == "Short") and (halMode == "Both" or halMode == "Short")
// The per-BAR filter, and it is SHORTS ONLY. It ships off. Unlike the range gate, a bar filter rejecting a
// break still CONSUMES the day - the latch fires on the break, not on the entry.
halTrendOK = not halUseTrend or (not na(halEmaVal) and hal15C < halEmaVal)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- live-trade tracking (runs in BOTH modes)
// The engine keeps its own copy of the open trade instead of reading strategy.position_size, for two reasons:
// the netted position now belongs to three setups, and Indicator mode has no position at all. The simulation
// matches the orders exactly - entry at the 15m close (process_orders_on_close), exit when price trades the
// stop or the target, stop taking precedence when a single bar covers both, which is what the Strategy Tester
// assumes as well.
if halTrDir != 0 and bar_index > halEntBar
    halStopHit = halTrDir == 1 ? low <= halStp : high >= halStp
    halTpHit   = halTrDir == 1 ? high >= halTgt : low <= halTgt
    if halStopHit or halTpHit
        if halState == 1
            halState := halStopHit ? 2 : 3
        halTrDir := 0

// TIME STOP: flat after the Nth 15m candle from the entry. Counted in the engine's own candles, so it does not
// change with the chart timeframe. Off in the shipped config.
if halNewBar and halTrDir != 0
    halBars15 += 1
if halMaxBars > 0 and halTrDir != 0 and halBars15 >= halMaxBars
    if ordersOn
        strategy.close("HAL-L", comment = "time stop")
        strategy.close("HAL-S", comment = "time stop")
        strategy.close("HAL-RL", comment = "time stop")
        strategy.close("HAL-RS", comment = "time stop")
    if halState == 1
        halState := (halTrDir == 1 ? close < halEnt : close > halEnt) ? 2 : 3
    halTrDir := 0

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the break
// halBroke latches the day's first break, so anything after it is ignored. The break is a 15-MINUTE close
// beyond the level; the range candle itself can never be the breakout candle.
halBrkUp = runHAL and halNewBar and not halIsRangeBar and halLevels and halRangeOK and not halBroke and hal15C > halRH
halBrkDn = runHAL and halNewBar and not halIsRangeBar and halLevels and halRangeOK and not halBroke and hal15C < halRL
// The first break consumes the day whichever side it fires on, and whether or not it passes its filters, so a
// filter can only ever REMOVE a trade, never substitute a later one.
if halBrkUp or halBrkDn
    halBroke := true

// The seat: Halyard is a market order at the 15m close and cannot rest, so a live ORB/IB trade does not delay
// it - it cancels it, and the break is still consumed. Same treatment as any other rejected filter.
// TWO reads of the same fact, because neither is enough on its own: orbibLive is the ORB/IB engines' own fill
// tracking, which is a chart bar stale here (those engines run below this one) but is all Indicator mode has;
// strategy.position_size is exact but only exists when orders are actually being placed. Halyard's own trade
// can never be the one showing in it - halTrDir == 0 is required below before any entry is considered.
halSeatFree = not orbibLive and not dayHalt and (not ordersOn or strategy.position_size == 0)
halEntered  = false
halEntDir   = 0

// --- First trade (take the FIRST breakout, if it passes the filters) ---
halEnterL = halBrkUp and halLongOK and halDayOK and halSeatFree and halTrades < halMaxTrades and halTrDir == 0 and halState == 0
if halEnterL
    sl = f_halLongStop(hal15C)
    tp = f_halLongTP(hal15C, sl, halRR)
    q  = f_halQty(hal15C, sl)
    halFirstDir := 1
    halState  := 1
    halTrades += 1
    halTrDir  := 1
    halEnt    := hal15C
    halStp    := sl
    halTgt    := tp
    halQty    := q
    halEntBar := bar_index
    halBars15 := 0
    halEntered := true
    halEntDir  := 1
    if ordersOn
        strategy.entry("HAL-L", strategy.long, qty = q)
        strategy.exit("HAL-Lx", from_entry = "HAL-L", stop = sl, limit = tp)

halEnterS = halBrkDn and halShortOK and halDayOK and halTrendOK and halSeatFree and halTrades < halMaxTrades and halTrDir == 0 and halState == 0
if halEnterS
    sl = f_halShortStop(hal15C)
    tp = f_halShortTP(hal15C, sl, halRR)
    q  = f_halQty(hal15C, sl)
    halFirstDir := -1
    halState  := 1
    halTrades += 1
    halTrDir  := -1
    halEnt    := hal15C
    halStp    := sl
    halTgt    := tp
    halQty    := q
    halEntBar := bar_index
    halBars15 := 0
    halEntered := true
    halEntDir  := -1
    if ordersOn
        strategy.entry("HAL-S", strategy.short, qty = q)
        strategy.exit("HAL-Sx", from_entry = "HAL-S", stop = sl, limit = tp)

// --- Reversal trade (only if the FIRST trade closed at a LOSS) ---
// OFF BY DEFAULT: Enable Reverse Trade ships unticked, so neither branch fires and the day's cap is 1 fill
// until someone ticks it. Ticking it also makes the Risk:Reward (Reverse Trade) input live.
// NOT filtered. The reversal is gated on the day-of-week, the direction and the losing first trade only - the
// entry filters apply to the FIRST trade. Note the per-day direction grid DOES reach it: a weekday set to one
// side can never take the reversal, since the reversal is by definition the opposite side of the loser.
halRevL = halRevOn and runHAL and halNewBar and halState == 2 and halFirstDir == -1 and halLongOK and halDayOK and halSeatFree and halTrades < halMaxTrades and halTrDir == 0 and halLevels and hal15C > halRH
if halRevL
    sl = f_halLongStop(hal15C)
    tp = f_halLongTP(hal15C, sl, halRevRR)
    q  = f_halQty(hal15C, sl)
    halState  := 3
    halTrades += 1
    halTrDir  := 1
    halEnt    := hal15C
    halStp    := sl
    halTgt    := tp
    halQty    := q
    halEntBar := bar_index
    halBars15 := 0
    halEntered := true
    halEntDir  := 1
    if ordersOn
        strategy.entry("HAL-RL", strategy.long, qty = q)
        strategy.exit("HAL-RLx", from_entry = "HAL-RL", stop = sl, limit = tp)

halRevS = halRevOn and runHAL and halNewBar and halState == 2 and halFirstDir == 1 and halShortOK and halDayOK and halSeatFree and halTrades < halMaxTrades and halTrDir == 0 and halLevels and hal15C < halRL
if halRevS
    sl = f_halShortStop(hal15C)
    tp = f_halShortTP(hal15C, sl, halRevRR)
    q  = f_halQty(hal15C, sl)
    halState  := 3
    halTrades += 1
    halTrDir  := -1
    halEnt    := hal15C
    halStp    := sl
    halTgt    := tp
    halQty    := q
    halEntBar := bar_index
    halBars15 := 0
    halEntered := true
    halEntDir  := -1
    if ordersOn
        strategy.entry("HAL-RS", strategy.short, qty = q)
        strategy.exit("HAL-RSx", from_entry = "HAL-RS", stop = sl, limit = tp)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Halyard end-of-day flat
// Never carry a position past the session its levels belong to, i.e. past 13:30 / 14:30 ET. This must fire on
// the LAST bar of that session; a Pine script cannot see the next bar, so it projects one CHART bar forward
// instead - exact on every ordinary boundary. halNewDay is the catch-up for boundaries inside a market gap.
//
// KNOWN GAP: that catch-up is NOT "one bar late". On a holiday early close the tape halts at 13:00 ET, BEFORE
// the boundary, so no flat fires and halNewDay does not arrive until the next session opens. On those ~10
// sessions a year the position is carried for hours. Watch those dates if you trade this live.
//
// This boundary is load-bearing: letting the position run to ET midnight instead leaves the morning's levels
// armed into the 18:00 ET Globex reopen, which is a different session, and those trades lose money.
//
// It closes HALYARD'S OWN entries only - an open ORB or IB trade is none of its business.
halDayFlat = halTrDir != 0 and (f_halSessionKey(time + chartMs) != halSessKey or halNewDay)
if halDayFlat
    if ordersOn
        strategy.close("HAL-L", comment = "day flat")
        strategy.close("HAL-S", comment = "day flat")
        strategy.close("HAL-RL", comment = "day flat")
        strategy.close("HAL-RS", comment = "day flat")
    if halState == 1
        halState := (halTrDir == 1 ? close < halEnt : close > halEnt) ? 2 : 3
    halTrDir := 0

// live Halyard trade -> the ORB and IB limits are pulled behind it (see the ORB/IB engines below)
halLive = halTrDir != 0

// shift the closed-15m-candle registers, AFTER everything above has read them as "the candles before this one"
if halNewBar
    hal15L2 := hal15L1
    hal15L1 := hal15L
    hal15H2 := hal15H1
    hal15H1 := hal15H

// ================================================================ Historical-probability stats (ORB / IB)
// TWO walk-forward studies are collected (a day is only added to the sample after its EOD flatten, so the
// numbers shown on any bar never contain data from that day or later):
//
//   A) FILL -> EOD, segmented by range size. One record per FILLED trade: did price TOUCH each level between
//      the fill and the EOD flatten? The fill is now the VWAP entry, so these rows describe what happens after
//      the trade this file actually takes. Range is stored as % of price (range / range-low * 100) so the
//      S/M/L buckets stay comparable as price drifts over the years. These are the "size" rows of the table.
//
//   B) PULLBACK -> EOD. RESEARCH ONLY, and no longer the entry: it still measures the 25% and 50% FIB
//      retracements, which this file no longer trades. Kept because the question it answers is still worth
//      having next to the VWAP entry - once price has retraced that far, how often does it go on to tag each
//      TP extension? One record per SETUP THAT BROKE its range (whether or not an order was actually placed).
//      On the very bar that reaches the pullback, a level counts only if the CLOSE is already beyond it. From
//      the next bar on, an ordinary wick touch counts. The 50% line can only be reached through the 25% line,
//      so the 50% sample is a subset of the 25% one.
f_pct(int hit, int n) => n > 0 ? 100.0 * hit / n : na
f_pctStr(int hit, int n) =>
    p = f_pct(hit, n)
    na(p) ? "-" : str.tostring(p, "#") + "%"

// ---- study A: one record per filled trade ----
var tRng   = array.new_float(0)
var tStrat = array.new_int(0)
var tSL100 = array.new_int(0)
var tSL75  = array.new_int(0)
var tTP0   = array.new_int(0)
var tTP10  = array.new_int(0)
var tTP30  = array.new_int(0)
var tTP50  = array.new_int(0)

f_pushTrade(int s, float rng, bool s100, bool s75, bool t0, bool t10, bool t30, bool t50) =>
    array.push(tRng,   rng)
    array.push(tStrat, s)
    array.push(tSL100, s100 ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tSL75,  s75  ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP0,   t0   ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP10,  t10  ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP30,  t30  ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(tTP50,  t50  ? 1 : 0)

// ranges recorded so far for one strategy (walk-forward: only days finalized before now)
f_ranges(int s) =>
    tmp = array.new_float(0)
    if array.size(tRng) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(tRng) - 1
            if array.get(tStrat, i) == s
                array.push(tmp, array.get(tRng, i))
    tmp

// tercile boundaries for a strategy (na until >=3 samples); in manual mode the caller passes fixed thresholds
f_b1(array<float> rr) => array.size(rr) < 3 ? na : array.percentile_linear_interpolation(rr, 33.33333)
f_b2(array<float> rr) => array.size(rr) < 3 ? na : array.percentile_linear_interpolation(rr, 66.66667)
f_bkt(float rng, float b1, float b2) => (na(b1) or na(b2)) ? 0 : rng < b1 ? 0 : rng < b2 ? 1 : 2

// counts [n, sl100, sl75, tp0, tp10, tp30, tp50] for one strategy+bucket given the boundaries
f_seg(int s, int bkt, float b1, float b2) =>
    nn = 0
    a0 = 0
    a1 = 0
    a2 = 0
    a3 = 0
    a4 = 0
    a5 = 0
    if array.size(tRng) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(tRng) - 1
            if array.get(tStrat, i) == s and f_bkt(array.get(tRng, i), b1, b2) == bkt
                nn := nn + 1
                a0 := a0 + array.get(tSL100, i)
                a1 := a1 + array.get(tSL75,  i)
                a2 := a2 + array.get(tTP0,   i)
                a3 := a3 + array.get(tTP10,  i)
                a4 := a4 + array.get(tTP30,  i)
                a5 := a5 + array.get(tTP50,  i)
    [nn, a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5]

// ---- study B: one record per armed setup, conditioned on how deep the pullback went ----
// Level order used everywhere below: 0 TP0, 1 TP10, 2 TP30, 3 TP50, 4 SL75, 5 SL100.
var pbStrat = array.new_int(0)
var pbRngP  = array.new_float(0)
var pbR25   = array.new_int(0)      // did price retrace to the 25% fib
var pbR50   = array.new_int(0)      // ... and to the 50% fib
var pb25_0  = array.new_int(0)      // levels reached from the 25% retrace onward
var pb25_1  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_2  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_3  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_4  = array.new_int(0)
var pb25_5  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_0  = array.new_int(0)      // levels reached from the 50% retrace onward
var pb50_1  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_2  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_3  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_4  = array.new_int(0)
var pb50_5  = array.new_int(0)

f_pbPush(int s, float rngP, bool r25, bool r50, array<bool> h25, array<bool> h50) =>
    array.push(pbStrat, s)
    array.push(pbRngP,  rngP)
    array.push(pbR25,   r25 ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pbR50,   r50 ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_0, array.get(h25, 0) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_1, array.get(h25, 1) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_2, array.get(h25, 2) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_3, array.get(h25, 3) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_4, array.get(h25, 4) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb25_5, array.get(h25, 5) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_0, array.get(h50, 0) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_1, array.get(h50, 1) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_2, array.get(h50, 2) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_3, array.get(h50, 3) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_4, array.get(h50, 4) ? 1 : 0)
    array.push(pb50_5, array.get(h50, 5) ? 1 : 0)

// counts for one strategy at one pullback depth. depth 0 = reached the 25% fib, 1 = reached the 50% fib.
// bkt = -1 pools all range sizes; 0/1/2 restricts to the S/M/L bucket defined by b1/b2.
// Returns [setups armed, setups that reached that pullback, then TP0, TP10, TP30, TP50, SL75, SL100 counts].
f_pbSeg(int s, int depth, int bkt, float b1, float b2) =>
    nAll = 0
    nn   = 0
    h0 = 0
    h1 = 0
    h2 = 0
    h3 = 0
    h4 = 0
    h5 = 0
    if array.size(pbStrat) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(pbStrat) - 1
            if array.get(pbStrat, i) == s and (bkt < 0 or f_bkt(array.get(pbRngP, i), b1, b2) == bkt)
                nAll := nAll + 1
                if (depth == 0 ? array.get(pbR25, i) : array.get(pbR50, i)) == 1
                    nn := nn + 1
                    h0 := h0 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_0, i) : array.get(pb50_0, i))
                    h1 := h1 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_1, i) : array.get(pb50_1, i))
                    h2 := h2 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_2, i) : array.get(pb50_2, i))
                    h3 := h3 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_3, i) : array.get(pb50_3, i))
                    h4 := h4 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_4, i) : array.get(pb50_4, i))
                    h5 := h5 + (depth == 0 ? array.get(pb25_5, i) : array.get(pb50_5, i))
    [nAll, nn, h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5]

// ================================================================ ORB ENGINE  (entry = 09:30 anchored VWAP)
var float or_rH = na
var float or_rL = na
var int   or_rHbar = na
var int   or_rLbar = na
var int   or_dir = 0
var float or_zstop = na
var float or_rng = na
var bool  or_broke = false
var bool  or_placed = false      // the setup has been armed at least once (drives the drawings)
var bool  or_f1 = false
var float or_fillPx = na         // the VWAP AS IT STOOD on the bar that filled - the level moves, so it is stored
var float or_fillQty = na        // ... and so does the risk-sized contract count
// THE ORDER THAT IS ACTUALLY ON THE BOOK. process_orders_on_close means an entry priced during a bar is only
// submitted at that bar's close, so it can first fill on the NEXT bar - against the price it was given, not
// against wherever the VWAP has drifted to by then. These two registers hold that resting price and quantity so
// the engine's own fill tracking tests exactly what the broker tests. na = nothing on the book.
var float or_restPx = na
var float or_restQty = na
var float or_avgPx = na
var float or_curStop = na
var float or_curTP = na
var bool  or_beDone = false
var bool  or_closed = false
var bool  or_oppBroke = false
var bool  or_missed = false      // the VWAP traded through while another setup held the seat

if newSession
    or_rH := na
    or_rL := na
    or_dir := 0
    or_zstop := na
    or_rng := na
    or_broke := false
    or_placed := false
    or_f1 := false
    or_fillPx := na
    or_fillQty := na
    or_restPx := na
    or_restQty := na
    or_avgPx := na
    or_curStop := na
    or_curTP := na
    or_beDone := false
    or_closed := false
    or_oppBroke := false
    or_missed := false
if or_inR
    if na(or_rH) or high > or_rH
        or_rH := high
        or_rHbar := bar_index
    if na(or_rL) or low < or_rL
        or_rL := low
        or_rLbar := bar_index
// Direction and stop are decided exactly as before - which extreme came first, plus the close-depth filter.
// What is NOT decided here any more is the entry price: it is not a property of the range at all now.
if or_rDone and not na(or_rH) and or_rH > or_rL
    or_rng := or_rH - or_rL
    or_lf = or_rLbar < or_rHbar
    or_pos = (close[1] - or_rL) / or_rng
    orbDepF = orbDepth / 100.0                    // how deep the close may sit, measured from the breaking level
    if orbLong and or_lf and or_pos >= 1.0 - orbDepF
        or_dir := 1
        or_zstop := f_sl(1, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, orbSl)
    else if orbShort and (not or_lf) and or_pos <= orbDepF
        or_dir := -1
        or_zstop := f_sl(-1, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, orbSl)

// ---- THE ENTRY, RE-PRICED EVERY BAR ----
// or_e1 is the anchored VWAP as it stands on THIS bar, not a level frozen when the range closed. Everything
// downstream - the stop distance, the contract count, the resting limit, the R/R box - is therefore recomputed
// bar by bar until the fill.
float or_e1 = or_dir != 0 ? avwap : na
// Signed distance from the entry to the stop: positive only while the VWAP is on the tradeable side of it.
float or_stopDist = (na(or_e1) or na(or_zstop)) ? na : (or_dir == 1 ? or_e1 - or_zstop : or_zstop - or_e1)
// The entry is only valid while the VWAP is far enough inside the range from the stop. A VWAP that has drifted
// onto or past the far edge would mean entering at or beyond its own stop, and would send the risk-$ sizer's
// contract count to infinity as the distance goes to zero. See orbibMinStopFrac in the config block.
bool or_entOK = not na(or_stopDist) and not na(or_rng) and or_rng > 0 and or_stopDist >= orbibMinStopFrac * or_rng
float orbSz1 = na
if or_entOK
    orbSz1 := sizeByRisk ? f_size(orbRiskDlr1, or_stopDist) : orbQty1

// break by selected type
or_brk = orbBreak == "Wick (touch)" ? ((or_dir == 1 and high >= or_rH) or (or_dir == -1 and low <= or_rL)) : ((or_dir == 1 and close > or_rH) or (or_dir == -1 and close < or_rL))
if or_dir != 0 and or_brk
    or_broke := true
// double-break detection: opposite range extreme is violated
if or_dir == 1 and low < or_rL
    or_oppBroke := true
if or_dir == -1 and high > or_rH
    or_oppBroke := true
// entry window: before IB forms (when IB is on), within ORB cutoff otherwise, on an allowed weekday
orbSizeOK = orbMinRngPct <= 0 or (not na(or_rng) and or_rL > 0 and or_rng / or_rL * 100 >= orbMinRngPct)
orbWin = inSess and not dayHalt and orbDayOK and tod <= (orbCutH*60 + orbCutM) and (not runIB or not ibFormed) and orbSizeOK
// CARRY: with the option armed, the limit survives the IB forming and KEEPS TRACKING THE VWAP - a stale frozen
// level would be worse than useless here. It still dies at the ORB cutoff, on a double-break, on the daily halt
// or at the flatten, and it gives way as soon as the IB arms its own setup (handled after the IB engine below).
orbHold = orbCarry and or_placed and not or_f1 and inSess and not dayHalt and orbDayOK and tod <= (orbCutH*60 + orbCutM)
// The window in which the ORB limit is allowed to rest at all.
orbRest = orbWin or orbHold
// SEAT: a live HALYARD trade pulls the ORB limit rather than leaving it resting. If price touches the VWAP
// during the hold, that entry was missed and the ORB is done for the day.
if runORB and or_dir != 0 and or_broke and not or_f1 and not or_closed and halLive and not na(or_e1)
    if (or_dir == 1 and low <= or_e1) or (or_dir == -1 and high >= or_e1)
        or_missed := true
// FILL FIRST, then re-price. This bar is tested against the order that was ALREADY on the book when it opened
// - the price set at the previous bar's close - which is the same thing the broker tests. Checking this bar's
// own VWAP instead would fill a break bar that reaches back to a level the order had not been given yet.
if not or_f1 and not or_closed and or_dir != 0 and not na(or_restPx)
    if (or_dir == 1 and low <= or_restPx) or (or_dir == -1 and high >= or_restPx)
        or_f1 := true
        or_fillPx := or_restPx
        or_fillQty := or_restQty
        or_avgPx := or_restPx
// ARM / RE-PRICE. Unlike the fib version this runs EVERY bar while the setup is live and unfilled, because the
// level moves. strategy.entry with the same id AMENDS the resting order - it does not stack a second one. The
// price it is given here is what the next bar will be filled against.
orbArm = runORB and or_dir != 0 and or_broke and not or_f1 and not or_closed and orbRest and not flatten and (not noDbl or not or_oppBroke) and or_entOK and orbSz1 >= 1 and not halLive and not or_missed
if orbArm
    if ordersOn
        if or_dir == 1
            strategy.entry("ORL", strategy.long, qty = orbSz1, limit = or_e1)
        else
            strategy.entry("ORS", strategy.short, qty = orbSz1, limit = or_e1)
    or_placed := true
    or_restPx := or_e1
    or_restQty := orbSz1
else
    or_restPx := na          // nothing resting: filled, held back, cancelled or out of its window
    or_restQty := na
or_firstFill = or_f1 and not or_f1[1]
if or_firstFill
    or_curStop := or_zstop
    or_curTP := f_tpGuard(or_dir, f_tp(or_dir, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, dHigh, dLow, or_fillPx, avwapDev, orbTpL, orbTpS), or_fillPx, or_zstop)
    or_beDone := false
if orbBE and not or_beDone and or_f1 and not or_closed
    if or_dir == 1 and high >= or_rH
        or_curStop := math.max(or_curStop, or_avgPx)
        or_beDone := true
    if or_dir == -1 and low <= or_rL
        or_curStop := math.min(or_curStop, or_avgPx)
        or_beDone := true
if ordersOn and not na(or_curStop)
    strategy.exit("ORLx", from_entry = "ORL", stop = or_curStop, limit = or_curTP)
    strategy.exit("ORSx", from_entry = "ORS", stop = or_curStop, limit = or_curTP)
if or_f1 and not or_closed and not na(or_curStop)
    if or_dir == 1 and (low <= or_curStop or high >= or_curTP)
        or_closed := true
    if or_dir == -1 and (high >= or_curStop or low <= or_curTP)
        or_closed := true
// Cancel the resting entry once it is done, flat, off, missed, on a double-break, out of its resting window, or
// while a Halyard trade holds the seat. halLive is in this list because the limit MOVES: leaving a stale order
// on the book behind an open Halyard trade is what would let two setups fill at once.
if ordersOn and (or_closed or flatten or not runORB or or_missed or halLive or (noDbl and or_oppBroke) or ((not orbRest) and not or_f1))
    strategy.cancel("ORL")
    strategy.cancel("ORS")

// ---- ORB study A: from the fill to EOD, did price touch each level? ----
var bool  or_trk    = false
var int   or_tdir   = 0
var float orL_sl100 = na
var float orL_sl75  = na
var float orL_tp0   = na
var float orL_tp10  = na
var float orL_tp30  = na
var float orL_tp50  = na
var bool  orR_sl100 = false
var bool  orR_sl75  = false
var bool  orR_tp0   = false
var bool  orR_tp10  = false
var bool  orR_tp30  = false
var bool  orR_tp50  = false
if newSession
    or_trk := false
if or_firstFill and not na(or_rng)
    or_trk    := true
    or_tdir   := or_dir
    orL_sl100 := or_dir == 1 ? or_rL : or_rH
    orL_sl75  := or_rL + (or_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * or_rng
    orL_tp0   := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH : or_rL
    orL_tp10  := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.10*or_rng : or_rL - 0.10*or_rng
    orL_tp30  := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.30*or_rng : or_rL - 0.30*or_rng
    orL_tp50  := or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.50*or_rng : or_rL - 0.50*or_rng
    orR_sl100 := false
    orR_sl75  := false
    orR_tp0   := false
    orR_tp10  := false
    orR_tp30  := false
    orR_tp50  := false
if or_trk
    if or_tdir == 1
        orR_tp0   := orR_tp0   or high >= orL_tp0
        orR_tp10  := orR_tp10  or high >= orL_tp10
        orR_tp30  := orR_tp30  or high >= orL_tp30
        orR_tp50  := orR_tp50  or high >= orL_tp50
        orR_sl75  := orR_sl75  or low  <= orL_sl75
        orR_sl100 := orR_sl100 or low  <= orL_sl100
    else
        orR_tp0   := orR_tp0   or low  <= orL_tp0
        orR_tp10  := orR_tp10  or low  <= orL_tp10
        orR_tp30  := orR_tp30  or low  <= orL_tp30
        orR_tp50  := orR_tp50  or low  <= orL_tp50
        orR_sl75  := orR_sl75  or high >= orL_sl75
        orR_sl100 := orR_sl100 or high >= orL_sl100
    if flatten
        f_pushTrade(0, or_rng / or_rL * 100, orR_sl100, orR_sl75, orR_tp0, orR_tp10, orR_tp30, orR_tp50)
        or_trk := false

// ---- ORB study B: armed -> 25% / 50% pullback -> which levels print from there, filed at the EOD flatten ----
// RESEARCH ONLY - these fib depths are no longer the entry. See the study-B note above.
var bool  orP_act  = false
var int   orP_dir  = 0
var float orP_rngP = na
var float orP_p25  = na
var float orP_p50  = na
var bool  orP_r25  = false
var bool  orP_r50  = false
var orP_lv  = array.new_float(6, na)      // 0 TP0, 1 TP10, 2 TP30, 3 TP50, 4 SL75, 5 SL100
var orP_h25 = array.new_bool(6, false)
var orP_h50 = array.new_bool(6, false)
if newSession
    orP_act := false
if or_broke and not or_broke[1] and or_dir != 0 and not na(or_rng) and or_rL > 0
    orP_act  := true
    orP_dir  := or_dir
    orP_rngP := or_rng / or_rL * 100
    orP_p25  := or_rL + (or_dir == 1 ? 0.75 : 0.25) * or_rng
    orP_p50  := or_rL + 0.50 * or_rng
    orP_r25  := false
    orP_r50  := false
    array.set(orP_lv, 0, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH : or_rL)
    array.set(orP_lv, 1, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.10*or_rng : or_rL - 0.10*or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 2, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.30*or_rng : or_rL - 0.30*or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 3, or_dir == 1 ? or_rH + 0.50*or_rng : or_rL - 0.50*or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 4, or_rL + (or_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * or_rng)
    array.set(orP_lv, 5, or_dir == 1 ? or_rL : or_rH)
    for k = 0 to 5
        array.set(orP_h25, k, false)
        array.set(orP_h50, k, false)
if orP_act
    up    = orP_dir == 1
    new25 = false
    new50 = false
    if not orP_r25 and (up ? low <= orP_p25 : high >= orP_p25)
        orP_r25 := true
        new25    := true
    if not orP_r50 and (up ? low <= orP_p50 : high >= orP_p50)
        orP_r50 := true
        new50    := true
    // On the bar that REACHES the pullback the touch must be confirmed by the CLOSE: the last tick of that bar
    // is beyond the level, so it traded there after the retrace. Later bars count an ordinary wick touch.
    for k = 0 to 5
        lv   = array.get(orP_lv, k)
        isTp = k <= 3
        wick = isTp ? (up ? high >= lv : low <= lv) : (up ? low <= lv : high >= lv)
        cls  = isTp ? (up ? close >= lv : close <= lv) : (up ? close <= lv : close >= lv)
        if orP_r25 and (new25 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(orP_h25, k, true)
        if orP_r50 and (new50 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(orP_h50, k, true)
    if flatten
        f_pbPush(0, orP_rngP, orP_r25, orP_r50, orP_h25, orP_h50)
        orP_act := false

// ================================================================ IB ENGINE  (entry = 09:30 anchored VWAP)
var float ib_rH = na
var float ib_rL = na
var int   ib_rHbar = na
var int   ib_rLbar = na
var int   ib_dir = 0
var float ib_zstop = na
var float ib_rng = na
var bool  ib_broke = false
var bool  ib_placed = false
var bool  ib_f1 = false
var float ib_fillPx = na
var float ib_fillQty = na
// The order actually on the book, priced at the previous bar's close. See the ORB engine's note.
var float ib_restPx = na
var float ib_restQty = na
var float ib_avgPx = na
var float ib_curStop = na
var float ib_curTP = na
var bool  ib_beDone = false
var bool  ib_closed = false
var bool  ib_oppBroke = false
var bool  ib_missed = false      // the VWAP was reached while another setup held the seat -> skip IB today

if newSession
    ib_rH := na
    ib_rL := na
    ib_dir := 0
    ib_zstop := na
    ib_rng := na
    ib_broke := false
    ib_placed := false
    ib_f1 := false
    ib_fillPx := na
    ib_fillQty := na
    ib_restPx := na
    ib_restQty := na
    ib_avgPx := na
    ib_curStop := na
    ib_curTP := na
    ib_beDone := false
    ib_closed := false
    ib_oppBroke := false
    ib_missed := false
if ib_inR
    if na(ib_rH) or high > ib_rH
        ib_rH := high
        ib_rHbar := bar_index
    if na(ib_rL) or low < ib_rL
        ib_rL := low
        ib_rLbar := bar_index
if ib_rDone and not na(ib_rH) and ib_rH > ib_rL
    ib_rng := ib_rH - ib_rL
    ib_lf = ib_rLbar < ib_rHbar
    ib_pos = (close[1] - ib_rL) / ib_rng
    ibDepF = ibDepth / 100.0
    if ibLong and ib_lf and ib_pos >= 1.0 - ibDepF
        ib_dir := 1
        ib_zstop := f_sl(1, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, ibSl)
    else if ibShort and (not ib_lf) and ib_pos <= ibDepF
        ib_dir := -1
        ib_zstop := f_sl(-1, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, ibSl)

// ---- THE ENTRY, RE-PRICED EVERY BAR (same rule as the ORB, same VWAP) ----
float ib_e1 = ib_dir != 0 ? avwap : na
float ib_stopDist = (na(ib_e1) or na(ib_zstop)) ? na : (ib_dir == 1 ? ib_e1 - ib_zstop : ib_zstop - ib_e1)
bool ib_entOK = not na(ib_stopDist) and not na(ib_rng) and ib_rng > 0 and ib_stopDist >= orbibMinStopFrac * ib_rng
float ibSz1 = na
if ib_entOK
    ibSz1 := sizeByRisk ? f_size(ibRiskDlr1, ib_stopDist) : ibQty1

// SEAT: an OPEN trade of ANY other setup keeps priority - the IB order is pulled (either direction, so the two
// can never stack risk or hedge each other). The IB is not written off, only delayed: the moment the seat frees
// the limit goes back in at the current VWAP, provided price has NOT already touched the VWAP while it was
// held. If it has, that entry was missed and the IB is done for the day.
orbLive   = runORB and or_f1 and not or_closed
ibHeld    = orbLive or halLive
ib_brk = ibBreak == "Wick (touch)" ? ((ib_dir == 1 and high >= ib_rH) or (ib_dir == -1 and low <= ib_rL)) : ((ib_dir == 1 and close > ib_rH) or (ib_dir == -1 and close < ib_rL))
if ib_dir != 0 and ib_brk
    ib_broke := true
if ib_dir == 1 and low < ib_rL
    ib_oppBroke := true
if ib_dir == -1 and high > ib_rH
    ib_oppBroke := true
ibWin = inSess and not dayHalt and ibDayOK and tod <= (ibCutH*60 + ibCutM)
// hold the IB while another trade is live; if the VWAP is touched during the hold, the IB is forfeited
if runIB and ib_dir != 0 and ib_broke and not ib_f1 and not ib_closed and ibHeld and not na(ib_e1)
    if (ib_dir == 1 and low <= ib_e1) or (ib_dir == -1 and high >= ib_e1)
        ib_missed := true
// FILL FIRST against the order already on the book, then re-price - exactly as in the ORB engine.
if not ib_f1 and not ib_closed and ib_dir != 0 and not na(ib_restPx)
    if (ib_dir == 1 and low <= ib_restPx) or (ib_dir == -1 and high >= ib_restPx)
        ib_f1 := true
        ib_fillPx := ib_restPx
        ib_fillQty := ib_restQty
        ib_avgPx := ib_restPx
// ARM / RE-PRICE, every bar, exactly as in the ORB engine
ibArm = runIB and ib_dir != 0 and ib_broke and not ib_f1 and not ib_closed and ibWin and not flatten and (not noDbl or not ib_oppBroke) and ib_entOK and ibSz1 >= 1 and not ibHeld and not ib_missed
if ibArm
    if ordersOn
        if ib_dir == 1
            strategy.entry("IBL", strategy.long, qty = ibSz1, limit = ib_e1)
        else
            strategy.entry("IBS", strategy.short, qty = ibSz1, limit = ib_e1)
    ib_placed := true
    ib_restPx := ib_e1
    ib_restQty := ibSz1
else
    ib_restPx := na
    ib_restQty := na
ib_firstFill = ib_f1 and not ib_f1[1]
if ib_firstFill
    ib_curStop := ib_zstop
    ib_curTP := f_tpGuard(ib_dir, f_tp(ib_dir, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, dHigh, dLow, ib_fillPx, avwapDev, ibTpL, ibTpS), ib_fillPx, ib_zstop)
    ib_beDone := false
if ibBE and not ib_beDone and ib_f1 and not ib_closed
    if ib_dir == 1 and high >= ib_rH
        ib_curStop := math.max(ib_curStop, ib_avgPx)
        ib_beDone := true
    if ib_dir == -1 and low <= ib_rL
        ib_curStop := math.min(ib_curStop, ib_avgPx)
        ib_beDone := true
if ordersOn and not na(ib_curStop)
    strategy.exit("IBLx", from_entry = "IBL", stop = ib_curStop, limit = ib_curTP)
    strategy.exit("IBSx", from_entry = "IBS", stop = ib_curStop, limit = ib_curTP)
if ib_f1 and not ib_closed and not na(ib_curStop)
    if ib_dir == 1 and (low <= ib_curStop or high >= ib_curTP)
        ib_closed := true
    if ib_dir == -1 and (high >= ib_curStop or low <= ib_curTP)
        ib_closed := true
if ordersOn and (ib_closed or flatten or not runIB or ib_missed or ibHeld or (noDbl and ib_oppBroke) or ((not ibWin) and not ib_f1))
    strategy.cancel("IBL")
    strategy.cancel("IBS")

// CARRY hand-over: the moment the IB breaks its range and has a valid setup, a carried ORB limit that is still
// unfilled is dropped - the IB gets the seat. A carried ORB that HAS filled keeps it (see orbLive above).
if runORB and orbCarry and not or_closed and not or_f1 and ib_dir != 0 and ib_broke
    if ordersOn
        strategy.cancel("ORL")
        strategy.cancel("ORS")
    or_closed := true

// The seat as Halyard reads it on the NEXT chart bar (declared above the Halyard engine).
orbibLive := orbLive or (runIB and ib_f1 and not ib_closed)

// ---- IB study A: from the fill to EOD, did price touch each level? ----
var bool  ib_trk    = false
var int   ib_tdir   = 0
var float ibL_sl100 = na
var float ibL_sl75  = na
var float ibL_tp0   = na
var float ibL_tp10  = na
var float ibL_tp30  = na
var float ibL_tp50  = na
var bool  ibR_sl100 = false
var bool  ibR_sl75  = false
var bool  ibR_tp0   = false
var bool  ibR_tp10  = false
var bool  ibR_tp30  = false
var bool  ibR_tp50  = false
if newSession
    ib_trk := false
if ib_firstFill and not na(ib_rng)
    ib_trk    := true
    ib_tdir   := ib_dir
    ibL_sl100 := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rL : ib_rH
    ibL_sl75  := ib_rL + (ib_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * ib_rng
    ibL_tp0   := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH : ib_rL
    ibL_tp10  := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.10*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.10*ib_rng
    ibL_tp30  := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.30*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.30*ib_rng
    ibL_tp50  := ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.50*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.50*ib_rng
    ibR_sl100 := false
    ibR_sl75  := false
    ibR_tp0   := false
    ibR_tp10  := false
    ibR_tp30  := false
    ibR_tp50  := false
if ib_trk
    if ib_tdir == 1
        ibR_tp0   := ibR_tp0   or high >= ibL_tp0
        ibR_tp10  := ibR_tp10  or high >= ibL_tp10
        ibR_tp30  := ibR_tp30  or high >= ibL_tp30
        ibR_tp50  := ibR_tp50  or high >= ibL_tp50
        ibR_sl75  := ibR_sl75  or low  <= ibL_sl75
        ibR_sl100 := ibR_sl100 or low  <= ibL_sl100
    else
        ibR_tp0   := ibR_tp0   or low  <= ibL_tp0
        ibR_tp10  := ibR_tp10  or low  <= ibL_tp10
        ibR_tp30  := ibR_tp30  or low  <= ibL_tp30
        ibR_tp50  := ibR_tp50  or low  <= ibL_tp50
        ibR_sl75  := ibR_sl75  or high >= ibL_sl75
        ibR_sl100 := ibR_sl100 or high >= ibL_sl100
    if flatten
        f_pushTrade(1, ib_rng / ib_rL * 100, ibR_sl100, ibR_sl75, ibR_tp0, ibR_tp10, ibR_tp30, ibR_tp50)
        ib_trk := false

// ---- IB study B: armed -> 25% / 50% pullback -> which levels print from there, filed at the EOD flatten ----
// RESEARCH ONLY - these fib depths are no longer the entry.
var bool  ibP_act  = false
var int   ibP_dir  = 0
var float ibP_rngP = na
var float ibP_p25  = na
var float ibP_p50  = na
var bool  ibP_r25  = false
var bool  ibP_r50  = false
var ibP_lv  = array.new_float(6, na)      // 0 TP0, 1 TP10, 2 TP30, 3 TP50, 4 SL75, 5 SL100
var ibP_h25 = array.new_bool(6, false)
var ibP_h50 = array.new_bool(6, false)
if newSession
    ibP_act := false
if ib_broke and not ib_broke[1] and ib_dir != 0 and not na(ib_rng) and ib_rL > 0
    ibP_act  := true
    ibP_dir  := ib_dir
    ibP_rngP := ib_rng / ib_rL * 100
    ibP_p25  := ib_rL + (ib_dir == 1 ? 0.75 : 0.25) * ib_rng
    ibP_p50  := ib_rL + 0.50 * ib_rng
    ibP_r25  := false
    ibP_r50  := false
    array.set(ibP_lv, 0, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH : ib_rL)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 1, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.10*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.10*ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 2, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.30*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.30*ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 3, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH + 0.50*ib_rng : ib_rL - 0.50*ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 4, ib_rL + (ib_dir == 1 ? 0.25 : 0.75) * ib_rng)
    array.set(ibP_lv, 5, ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rL : ib_rH)
    for k = 0 to 5
        array.set(ibP_h25, k, false)
        array.set(ibP_h50, k, false)
if ibP_act
    up    = ibP_dir == 1
    new25 = false
    new50 = false
    if not ibP_r25 and (up ? low <= ibP_p25 : high >= ibP_p25)
        ibP_r25 := true
        new25    := true
    if not ibP_r50 and (up ? low <= ibP_p50 : high >= ibP_p50)
        ibP_r50 := true
        new50    := true
    for k = 0 to 5
        lv   = array.get(ibP_lv, k)
        isTp = k <= 3
        wick = isTp ? (up ? high >= lv : low <= lv) : (up ? low <= lv : high >= lv)
        cls  = isTp ? (up ? close >= lv : close <= lv) : (up ? close <= lv : close >= lv)
        if ibP_r25 and (new25 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(ibP_h25, k, true)
        if ibP_r50 and (new50 ? cls : wick)
            array.set(ibP_h50, k, true)
    if flatten
        f_pbPush(1, ibP_rngP, ibP_r25, ibP_r50, ibP_h25, ibP_h50)
        ibP_act := false

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- EOD flatten + daily loss limit
// The 15:30 flatten closes the ORB/IB entries BY ID. Halyard has its own 13:30/14:30 ET boundary and closes its
// own entries there, so neither engine can ever flatten the other's trade.
if ordersOn and flatten
    strategy.close("ORL", comment = "EOD flat")
    strategy.close("ORS", comment = "EOD flat")
    strategy.close("IBL", comment = "EOD flat")
    strategy.close("IBS", comment = "EOD flat")
// The daily max loss is the ONE rule that reaches across setups: it is an account circuit breaker, so it closes
// everything that is open, Halyard included, and cancels every resting order.
if dayHalt
    if ordersOn
        strategy.close_all(comment = "Daily max loss")
        strategy.cancel_all()
    halTrDir := 0

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Automation: PickMyTrade webhook (net position)
// PickMyTrade's documented alert schema carries the buy/sell/close instruction in a field called "data".
// Earlier versions of this file sent it as "action" only. Both are emitted here, with the same value: "data"
// is the documented name, and "action" is kept so a setup that was already working on it keeps working. An
// unrecognised extra key is ignored by the endpoint; a MISSING one is not.
//
// sl and tp are ABSOLUTE PRICE LEVELS, not distances - 0 means "no level, use the account default".
//
// EVERY NUMBER GOES THROUGH f_num, and that is the bug fix that matters here. str.tostring(na) renders the
// four characters NaN, which is not valid JSON: one na stop or target and the whole payload is rejected at the
// far end, so the entry that was already accepted sits at the broker with no bracket on it. f_num turns an
// unknown level into 0 instead, which the schema accepts.
f_num(float v) => na(v) ? "0" : str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(v))

// `add` marks an ADD-ON to a position that is already open, and it changes three things in the payload:
//   quantity  - the CALLER sends the INCREMENT, not the net (see the quantity note below);
//   pyramid   - true lets PickMyTrade stack the fill onto the open position instead of treating a
//               second same-direction signal as a fresh position;
//   update_sl / update_tp - true amends the bracket already working on that symbol rather than
//               creating a second one, so the whole enlarged position ends up under ONE stop and
//               ONE target (both units of this strategy share the same two prices).
// same_direction_ignore is pinned false: a same-direction signal must never be silently dropped, or
// the add would vanish. reverse_order_close is pinned true so a direction flip flattens first - the
// seat rules mean that should never happen, but if it ever did, flattening is the safe reading.
f_pmt(string act, float q, float slp, float tpp, bool add) =>
    '{"token":"' + pmtToken + '","account_id":"' + pmtAcct + '","symbol":"' + pmtSym +
      '","data":"' + act + '","action":"' + act + '","quantity":' + str.tostring(q) +
      ',"order_type":"' + pmtType +
      '","sl":' + f_num(slp) +
      ',"tp":' + f_num(tpp) +
      ',"pyramid":' + (add ? "true" : "false") +
      ',"same_direction_ignore":false,"reverse_order_close":true' +
      ',"update_sl":' + (add ? "true" : "false") +
      ',"update_tp":' + (add ? "true" : "false") + '}'

// WHICH setup's bracket to quote. This has to survive a lag: the alerts fire on a change in the NETTED
// strategy.position_size, and that variable only reflects a fill on the bar AFTER the engine books it, so by
// the time an alert goes out the setup that caused it may already have been closed and reset.
// The old chain was `halLive ? halStp : liveORB ? or_curStop : ib_curStop` - note the final branch is not
// guarded on the IB actually being in a trade, so any moment neither Halyard nor the ORB was live it resolved
// to ib_curStop, which is na on every day the IB never filled. That na is what became NaN in the JSON.
// Now: prefer whichever setup is genuinely live, and otherwise fall back to the bracket latched at the last
// fill, so the webhook always has a real pair of prices to quote.
liveORB  = or_f1 and not or_closed
liveIB   = ib_f1 and not ib_closed
var float lastStop = na
var float lastTgt  = na
if halEntered
    lastStop := halStp
    lastTgt  := halTgt
if or_firstFill
    lastStop := or_curStop
    lastTgt  := or_curTP
if ib_firstFill
    lastStop := ib_curStop
    lastTgt  := ib_curTP
autoStop = halLive ? halStp : liveORB ? or_curStop : liveIB ? ib_curStop : lastStop
autoTP   = halLive ? halTgt : liveORB ? or_curTP  : liveIB ? ib_curTP  : lastTgt
// QUANTITY: THE INCREMENT, NOT THE NET.
// This used to send math.abs(strategy.position_size) - the whole netted position - on every entry
// alert. On a first entry those are the same number, so it looked right. On the AVERAGE-DOWN fill it
// was not: holding 2 and adding 2, it transmitted "buy 4" to a broker that already had 2 on. A
// platform reading quantity as the position it should end up holding can only reconcile that by
// flattening the 2 and re-entering 4 - which realises the first unit's open loss at the worst moment
// and re-opens the whole thing at the current price, destroying the averaging-down the setup exists
// to do. What an add actually means is "buy 2 MORE", so that is what goes out now.
//   from flat        -> increment == net, unchanged behaviour
//   same-direction up -> the difference, flagged as an add so it stacks
//   direction flip    -> the NEW position size, with reverse_order_close doing the flattening
// A same-direction DECREASE (one unit's bracket fills while the other stays on) sends nothing, as
// before: the broker's own stop and target orders are what close the units, not these alerts.
posNow   = strategy.position_size
posPrev  = strategy.position_size[1]
sameDir  = posNow != 0 and posPrev != 0 and ((posNow > 0) == (posPrev > 0))
isAdd    = sameDir and math.abs(posNow) > math.abs(posPrev)
autoQty  = isAdd ? math.abs(posNow - posPrev) : math.abs(posNow)
buyNow   = posNow > 0 and (posPrev <= 0 or posNow > posPrev)
sellNow  = posNow < 0 and (posPrev >= 0 or posNow < posPrev)
closeNow = posNow == 0 and posPrev != 0
// The exact string that went out, kept for the on-chart debug readout below.
var string pmtLast = ""
if autoOn and ordersOn and buyNow
    pmtLast := f_pmt("buy",  autoQty, autoStop, autoTP, isAdd)
    alert(pmtLast, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
if autoOn and ordersOn and sellNow
    pmtLast := f_pmt("sell", autoQty, autoStop, autoTP, isAdd)
    alert(pmtLast, alert.freq_once_per_bar)
if autoOn and ordersOn and closeNow
    pmtLast := f_pmt("close", 0, 0.0, 0.0, false)
    alert(pmtLast, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ---- on-chart readout of the LAST payload, so you can read what was actually transmitted ----
// TradingView does not show you an alert()'s message after the fact, which is why a wrong or malformed payload
// is so hard to spot. This prints the most recent one on the chart. Check it shows a real number for both
// "sl" and "tp" - never NaN, and never 0 on a trade that is supposed to carry a bracket.
var label pmtLbl = na
if pmtDebug and barstate.islast and autoOn
    if not na(pmtLbl)
        label.delete(pmtLbl)
    pmtLbl := label.new(bar_index, high, str.length(pmtLast) > 0 ? "last webhook payload:\n" + pmtLast : "no webhook payload sent yet", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(color.navy, 10), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Break alerts (fire once when each range breaks)
// For ORB and IB the entry quoted is the VWAP AS IT STANDS ON THE BREAK BAR. It is not a fixed level - it will
// keep moving until the order fills, so treat it as "where the limit is right now", not "where it will fill".
if brkAlerts and runHAL and (halBrkUp or halBrkDn)
    halSLa = halBrkUp ? f_halLongStop(hal15C) : f_halShortStop(hal15C)
    halTPa = halBrkUp ? f_halLongTP(hal15C, halSLa, halRR) : f_halShortTP(hal15C, halSLa, halRR)
    alert("HALYARD 15m BREAK  " + (halBrkUp ? "LONG" : "SHORT") +
         "  | broke " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(halBrkUp ? halRH : halRL)) +
         "  | entry " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(hal15C)) +
         "  | stop " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(halSLa)) +
         "  | target " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(halTPa)), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
if brkAlerts and runORB and or_dir != 0 and or_broke and not or_broke[1]
    orTPa = f_tp(or_dir, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, dHigh, dLow, or_e1, avwapDev, orbTpL, orbTpS)
    alert("ORB BREAK  " + (or_dir == 1 ? "LONG" : "SHORT") +
         "  | broke " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(or_dir == 1 ? or_rH : or_rL)) +
         "  | VWAP entry now " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(or_e1)) + " (tracks the 09:30 VWAP)" +
         "  | stop " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(or_zstop)) +
         "  | target " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(orTPa)), alert.freq_once_per_bar)
if brkAlerts and runIB and ib_dir != 0 and ib_broke and not ib_broke[1]
    ibTPa = f_tp(ib_dir, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, dHigh, dLow, ib_e1, avwapDev, ibTpL, ibTpS)
    alert("IB BREAK  " + (ib_dir == 1 ? "LONG" : "SHORT") +
         "  | broke " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ib_dir == 1 ? ib_rH : ib_rL)) +
         "  | VWAP entry now " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ib_e1)) + " (tracks the 09:30 VWAP)" +
         "  | stop " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ib_zstop)) +
         "  | target " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ibTPa)), alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ================================================================ Risk/Reward + fib tool (ALL THREE SETUPS)
// ONE routine draws every setup's box, so Halyard, ORB and IB are read the same way: a GREEN box from the entry
// to the target, a RED box from the entry to the stop, a border in the setup's colour (orange ORB, teal IB,
// fuchsia Halyard) and one label with contracts, $ risk, $ reward, R multiple and the 1-contract numbers.
// ANCHORING: x is BAR INDEX, fixed at creation, and the right edge is extended bar by bar while the setup is
// live, so the box always covers real bars - it never projects into empty space past the last bar and never
// stretches across a session gap.
// PRICES ARE NOT FIXED ANY MORE. The ORB and IB entry rides the VWAP, so their boxes are RE-PRICED on every
// bar until the fill and freeze at the fill price. Halyard's entry is a 15m close, so its box never moves.
// HISTORY: every valid setup keeps its boxes and fib lines. Only the text labels are capped by default.
var array<box>   dBox = array.new<box>()
var array<line>  dLin = array.new<line>()
var array<label> dLab = array.new<label>()

// One setup now draws TWO boxes, THREE fib lines and ONE label (the average-down unit is gone with the fib
// entries), so the per-setup limits multiply out at those rates.
f_trimDraws() =>
    if keepBox > 0
        while array.size(dBox) > keepBox * 2
            box.delete(array.shift(dBox))
        while array.size(dLin) > keepBox * 3
            line.delete(array.shift(dLin))
    if keepLab > 0
        while array.size(dLab) > keepLab
            label.delete(array.shift(dLab))

// The label's text, split out of f_drawRR so the re-pricer can rebuild it with the same wording every bar.
// pv = $ per point per contract. ORB/IB pass the "$ per point" input; Halyard passes the symbol's own point
// value, which is what its position sizer divides by - so every box reports the money that setup actually risks.
f_rrText(float ent, float zstop, float ptp, float q, string tag, float pv) =>
    riskUsd = math.abs(ent - zstop) * pv * q
    rewUsd  = math.abs(ptp - ent) * pv * q
    risk1   = math.abs(ent - zstop) * pv
    rew1    = math.abs(ptp - ent) * pv
    rrr     = riskUsd > 0 ? rewUsd / riskUsd : na
    tag + "  " + str.tostring(q, "#.#") + " contract" + (q == 1 ? "" : "s") + " @ " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(ent)) +
     "\nRisk $" + str.tostring(riskUsd, "#") + " | Reward $" + str.tostring(rewUsd, "#") + " (" + str.tostring(rrr, "#.##") + "R)" +
     "\n1 contract: Risk $" + str.tostring(risk1, "#") + " | Reward $" + str.tostring(rew1, "#")

// Markup for ONE entry unit. d = 1 long, -1 short. q = contracts on this entry.
f_drawRR(int d, float ent, float zstop, float ptp, float q, color sigCol, string tag, float pv) =>
    bw = box.new(bar_index, d == 1 ? ptp : ent, bar_index + 1, d == 1 ? ent : ptp, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = sigCol, border_width = 1, bgcolor = color.new(color.green, 82))
    br = box.new(bar_index, d == 1 ? ent : zstop, bar_index + 1, d == 1 ? zstop : ent, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = sigCol, border_width = 1, bgcolor = color.new(color.red, 82))
    lb = label.new(bar_index + 1, ent, f_rrText(ent, zstop, ptp, q, tag, pv), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.gray, 15), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
    array.push(dBox, bw)
    array.push(dBox, br)
    array.push(dLab, lb)
    [bw, br, lb]

// Move an existing box pair and its label onto a NEW entry price. This is what makes a moving limit legible:
// while the VWAP drifts, the red risk box and green reward box grow and shrink around it and the $ figures in
// the label follow, so what you see is always the trade that would be taken if the limit filled right now.
f_repriceRR(box bw, box br, label lb, int d, float ent, float zstop, float ptp, float q, string tag, float pv) =>
    if not na(bw)
        box.set_top(bw,    d == 1 ? ptp : ent)
        box.set_bottom(bw, d == 1 ? ent : ptp)
        box.set_top(br,    d == 1 ? ent : zstop)
        box.set_bottom(br, d == 1 ? zstop : ent)
    if not na(lb)
        label.set_y(lb, ent)
        label.set_text(lb, f_rrText(ent, zstop, ptp, q, tag, pv))

f_drawFibs(float rL, float rg, color sigCol, array<line> dest) =>
    array.clear(dest)
    for i = 1 to 3
        y = rL + i * 0.25 * rg
        ln = line.new(bar_index, y, bar_index + 1, y, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(sigCol, 35), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        array.push(dest, ln)
        array.push(dLin, ln)

// stretch one live unit's drawings to the current bar
f_growUnit(box bw, box br, label lb) =>
    if not na(bw)
        box.set_right(bw, bar_index)
        box.set_right(br, bar_index)
        if not na(lb)
            label.set_x(lb, bar_index)

f_growFibs(array<line> fib) =>
    if array.size(fib) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(fib) - 1
            line.set_x2(array.get(fib, i), bar_index)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- ORB drawings
// Drawn when the ENTRY ORDER IS FIRST ARMED (or_placed / ib_placed), so a break that any filter rejects - wrong
// weekday, range too small, past the cutoff, IB already formed, double-break day, daily loss halt, sizing under
// one contract, a VWAP too close to the stop, or a limit held behind an open Halyard/ORB trade - draws nothing.
// The box is then RE-PRICED every bar while the limit is unfilled, because the entry is riding the VWAP.
var box   orbBw  = na
var box   orbBr  = na
var label orbLb  = na
var bool  orbGrow = false
var array<line> orbFib = array.new<line>()
if runORB and or_placed and not or_placed[1] and not na(or_e1) and not na(or_zstop)
    orTP = f_tpGuard(or_dir, f_tp(or_dir, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, dHigh, dLow, or_e1, avwapDev, orbTpL, orbTpS), or_e1, or_zstop)
    orbBw := na
    orbBr := na
    orbLb := na
    if showFibs
        f_drawFibs(or_rL, or_rng, color.new(color.orange, 0), orbFib)
    if showRR
        [bw, br, lb] = f_drawRR(or_dir, or_e1, or_zstop, orTP, orbSz1, color.new(color.orange, 0), "ORB @ VWAP", ptVal)
        orbBw := bw
        orbBr := br
        orbLb := lb
    orbGrow := true
    f_trimDraws()
if orbGrow
    f_growUnit(orbBw, orbBr, orbLb)
    f_growFibs(orbFib)
    // Before the fill the box tracks the live VWAP; from the fill on it is pinned to the price that filled.
    orbRrEnt = or_f1 ? or_fillPx : or_e1
    orbRrQty = or_f1 ? or_fillQty : orbSz1
    orbRrTP  = or_f1 ? or_curTP : f_tpGuard(or_dir, f_tp(or_dir, or_rH, or_rL, or_rng, dHigh, dLow, or_e1, avwapDev, orbTpL, orbTpS), or_e1, or_zstop)
    if not na(orbRrEnt) and not na(orbRrQty) and not na(or_zstop)
        f_repriceRR(orbBw, orbBr, orbLb, or_dir, orbRrEnt, or_zstop, orbRrTP, orbRrQty, "ORB @ VWAP", ptVal)
    if or_closed or flatten or (not or_f1 and not orbRest)
        orbGrow := false

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- IB drawings
var box   ibBw  = na
var box   ibBr  = na
var label ibLb  = na
var bool  ibGrow = false
var array<line> ibFib = array.new<line>()
if runIB and ib_placed and not ib_placed[1] and not na(ib_e1) and not na(ib_zstop)
    ibTP = f_tpGuard(ib_dir, f_tp(ib_dir, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, dHigh, dLow, ib_e1, avwapDev, ibTpL, ibTpS), ib_e1, ib_zstop)
    ibBw := na
    ibBr := na
    ibLb := na
    if showFibs
        f_drawFibs(ib_rL, ib_rng, color.new(color.teal, 0), ibFib)
    if showRR
        [bw2, br2, lb2] = f_drawRR(ib_dir, ib_e1, ib_zstop, ibTP, ibSz1, color.new(color.teal, 0), "IB @ VWAP", ptVal)
        ibBw := bw2
        ibBr := br2
        ibLb := lb2
    ibGrow := true
    f_trimDraws()
if ibGrow
    f_growUnit(ibBw, ibBr, ibLb)
    f_growFibs(ibFib)
    ibRrEnt = ib_f1 ? ib_fillPx : ib_e1
    ibRrQty = ib_f1 ? ib_fillQty : ibSz1
    ibRrTP  = ib_f1 ? ib_curTP : f_tpGuard(ib_dir, f_tp(ib_dir, ib_rH, ib_rL, ib_rng, dHigh, dLow, ib_e1, avwapDev, ibTpL, ibTpS), ib_e1, ib_zstop)
    if not na(ibRrEnt) and not na(ibRrQty) and not na(ib_zstop)
        f_repriceRR(ibBw, ibBr, ibLb, ib_dir, ibRrEnt, ib_zstop, ibRrTP, ibRrQty, "IB @ VWAP", ptVal)
    if ib_closed or flatten or (not ib_f1 and not ibWin)
        ibGrow := false

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- HALYARD drawings
// Same box, same label, same growth rule as the two above - only the border colour differs, and the prices
// never move because Halyard enters at a 15m close rather than on a resting limit. The money figures use the
// symbol's own point value, which is exactly what the Halyard position sizer divides by.
var box   halBw   = na
var box   halBr   = na
var label halLb   = na
var bool  halGrow = false
if runHAL and halEntered and showRR and showRRHal
    halBw := na
    halBr := na
    halLb := na
    [bwH, brH, lbH] = f_drawRR(halEntDir, halEnt, halStp, halTgt, halQty, halSigCol, halEntDir == 1 ? "HALYARD long" : "HALYARD short", syminfo.pointvalue)
    halBw := bwH
    halBr := brH
    halLb := lbH
    halGrow := true
    f_trimDraws()
if halGrow
    f_growUnit(halBw, halBr, halLb)
    if halTrDir == 0
        halGrow := false

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strategy rules panel (top-right)
var table info = na
if showInfo and barstate.islast
    info := table.new(position.top_right, 1, 18, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 15), border_color = color.new(color.gray, 50), border_width = 1)
    table.cell(info, 0, 0,  (ordersOn ? "" : "[INDICATOR - no orders]  ") + "HALYARD + BREAK-THEN-VWAP (ORB + IB)",
         text_color = ordersOn ? color.aqua : color.orange, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 1,  "HALYARD: 15m candles built from chart bars - any chart TF",  text_color = color.fuchsia, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 2,  "  range = the 00:00 EST / 01:00 EDT 15m candle",             text_color = color.silver,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 3,  "  first 15m CLOSE beyond it trades | stop = far edge | R:R " + str.tostring(halRR, "#.##"), text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 4,  "  one break per day | flat 13:30 / 14:30 ET",                text_color = color.silver,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 5,  "Ranges: ORB 09:30-09:45 | IB 09:30-10:30 (ET)",              text_color = color.white,   text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 6,  "Direction: low-first = LONG, high-first = SHORT",            text_color = color.white,   text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 7,  "  + close no deeper than " + str.tostring(orbDepth, "#") + "% (ORB) / " + str.tostring(ibDepth, "#") + "% (IB) into the range",
         text_color = color.silver, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 8,  "ENTRY: limit at the 09:30 ANCHORED VWAP",                    text_color = color.orange,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 9,  "  re-priced every bar - the limit rides the VWAP",           text_color = color.silver,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 10, "Stop: ORB " + orbSl + "  |  IB " + ibSl,                     text_color = color.white,   text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 11, "Target: ORB " + orbTpL + " L / " + orbTpS + " S  |  IB " + ibTpL + " L / " + ibTpS + " S", text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 12, "One unit per setup - no avg-down (VWAP is one price)",       text_color = color.silver,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 13, "SEAT: Halyard > ORB > IB - one trade at a time",             text_color = color.aqua,    text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 14, orbCarry ? "ORB carry ON: unfilled ORB rests past 10:30" : "ORB carry off (unfilled ORB dies at 10:30)", text_color = orbCarry ? color.orange : color.gray, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 15, "Skip double-break days | ORB/IB flatten 15:30 ET",           text_color = color.silver,  text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 16, "Toggle Run HAL / ORB / IB + weekdays to isolate results",    text_color = color.aqua,    text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(info, 0, 17, modeTxt + (maxDayLoss > 0 ? "  | day stop $" + str.tostring(maxDayLoss, "#") + (dayHalt ? " - HIT" : "") : "") + (rmFixed ? "" : " (per entry, fixed capital)"), text_color = dayHalt ? color.red : color.yellow, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Probability table (ORB / IB setups only)
// Columns: N = sample size, Reach = how often that starting point is even reached, then the odds of price
// trading to each level from that starting point, before the 15:30 flatten.
//   "From FILL" rows   : start = the entry fill, i.e. the VWAP touch, split by range size. Reach is n/a (the
//                        trade filled by definition).
//   "From 25/50% PB"   : RESEARCH ROWS, not the entry any more. Start = the moment price retraces to that fib
//                        depth of the range. Reach = share of armed setups that pull back that far. Kept so the
//                        old fib entry can still be compared against the VWAP one on the same chart.
// The level columns are FIXED research levels, not your settings: TP0/10/30/50 are the range edge and its
// extensions, "75% line" and "100% line" are the two retracement depths. They do not move when you change the
// target or stop dropdowns - that is the point, the table stays a constant yardstick you can re-read after
// every settings change. Read the column that matches the setting you are testing.
// Halyard is not in this table: it has no resting entry and no range-extension targets, so none of these rows
// would mean anything for it.
tPos  = tblPos == "Top right" ? position.top_right : tblPos == "Bottom left" ? position.bottom_left : tblPos == "Top left" ? position.top_left : position.bottom_right
tRows = 8 + (pbSplit ? 12 : 4)

var table probTbl = na

f_tblRow(int row, string lbl, int nn, string reach, int t0, int t1, int t2, int t3, int q75, int q100, color txt, color bg) =>
    table.cell(probTbl, 0, row, lbl,                text_color = txt,          bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(probTbl, 1, row, str.tostring(nn),   text_color = color.white,  bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 2, row, reach,              text_color = color.silver, bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 3, row, f_pctStr(t0,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 4, row, f_pctStr(t1,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 5, row, f_pctStr(t2,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 6, row, f_pctStr(t3,  nn),  text_color = color.lime,   bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 7, row, f_pctStr(q75, nn),  text_color = color.red,    bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(probTbl, 8, row, f_pctStr(q100, nn), text_color = color.red,    bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.normal)

// where we are right now, used to tint the row that applies (nothing is drawn on the chart)
cNow = color.new(color.blue, 40)      // the row that is live on this bar
cWas = color.new(color.blue, 78)      // a depth price has already passed through
cOff = color.black

if showTable and barstate.islast
    if na(probTbl)
        probTbl := table.new(tPos, 9, tRows, bgcolor = color.black, border_color = color.new(color.white, 70), border_width = 1, frame_color = color.white, frame_width = 1)
    // live state per strategy: 0 = not in play, 1 = broke, 2 = at the 25% pullback, 3 = at the 50% pullback
    stA  = array.from(orP_act ? (orP_r50 ? 3 : orP_r25 ? 2 : 1) : 0, ibP_act ? (ibP_r50 ? 3 : ibP_r25 ? 2 : 1) : 0)
    rgA  = array.from(orP_act ? orP_rngP : na, ibP_act ? ibP_rngP : na)
    filA = array.from((or_f1 and not or_closed) ? 1 : 0, (ib_f1 and not ib_closed) ? 1 : 0)
    hdr  = array.from("From FILL - by range size", "N", "Reach", "TP0", "TP10", "TP30", "TP50", "75% line", "100% line")
    for c = 0 to 8
        table.cell(probTbl, c, 0, array.get(hdr, c), text_color = color.black, bgcolor = color.white, text_size = size.normal, text_halign = c == 0 ? text.align_left : text.align_center)
    // ---- section 1: from the fill, segmented by range size ----
    for s = 0 to 1
        rr = f_ranges(s)
        b1 = autoMode ? f_b1(rr) : (s == 0 ? orbB1 : ibB1)
        b2 = autoMode ? f_b2(rr) : (s == 0 ? orbB2 : ibB2)
        nm = s == 0 ? "ORB" : "IB"
        s1 = na(b1) ? "?" : str.tostring(b1, "#.##") + "%"
        s2 = na(b2) ? "?" : str.tostring(b2, "#.##") + "%"
        for bkt = 0 to 2
            [nn, a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5] = f_seg(s, bkt, b1, b2)
            here = hiLive and array.get(stA, s) > 0 and not na(array.get(rgA, s)) and f_bkt(array.get(rgA, s), b1, b2) == bkt
            inTr = here and array.get(filA, s) == 1
            lbl  = (inTr ? "> " : "") + (bkt == 0 ? nm + " S <" + s1 : bkt == 1 ? nm + " M " + s1 + "-" + s2 : nm + " L >=" + s2)
            f_tblRow(s * 3 + bkt + 1, lbl, nn, "-", a2, a3, a4, a5, a1, a0, color.white, inTr ? cNow : here ? cWas : cOff)
    // ---- section 2: from the 25% / 50% pullback (research rows - not the entry) ----
    hdr2 = array.from("From PULLBACK (research)", "N", "Reach", "TP0", "TP10", "TP30", "TP50", "75% line", "100% line")
    for c = 0 to 8
        table.cell(probTbl, c, 7, array.get(hdr2, c), text_color = color.black, bgcolor = color.new(color.aqua, 20), text_size = size.normal, text_halign = c == 0 ? text.align_left : text.align_center)
    for s = 0 to 1
        rr2 = f_ranges(s)
        c1  = autoMode ? f_b1(rr2) : (s == 0 ? orbB1 : ibB1)
        c2  = autoMode ? f_b2(rr2) : (s == 0 ? orbB2 : ibB2)
        nm2 = s == 0 ? "ORB" : "IB"
        st  = array.get(stA, s)
        for d = 0 to 1
            // the deepest pullback price has reached is "now"; a shallower one it already passed is tinted faintly
            depthOn = hiLive and (d == 0 ? st >= 2 : st >= 3)
            isNow   = hiLive and (d == 0 ? st == 2 : st == 3)
            if pbSplit
                for bkt = 0 to 2
                    [nAll, nn, h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5] = f_pbSeg(s, d, bkt, c1, c2)
                    same = depthOn and not na(array.get(rgA, s)) and f_bkt(array.get(rgA, s), c1, c2) == bkt
                    szn  = bkt == 0 ? "S" : bkt == 1 ? "M" : "L"
                    lbl  = ((same and isNow) ? "> " : "") + nm2 + " " + szn + " from " + (d == 0 ? "25%" : "50%") + " PB"
                    f_tblRow(8 + s * 6 + bkt * 2 + d, lbl, nn, f_pctStr(nn, nAll), h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, d == 0 ? color.aqua : color.yellow, (same and isNow) ? cNow : same ? cWas : cOff)
            else
                [nAll, nn, h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5] = f_pbSeg(s, d, -1, c1, c2)
                lbl = (isNow ? "> " : "") + nm2 + " from " + (d == 0 ? "25%" : "50%") + " pullback"
                f_tblRow(8 + s * 2 + d, lbl, nn, f_pctStr(nn, nAll), h0, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, d == 0 ? color.aqua : color.yellow, isNow ? cNow : depthOn ? cWas : cOff)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Visuals
// THE ENTRY LEVEL. One line, drawn for the whole session, that both pullback setups rest their limit on.
plot(showVwap and inSess ? avwap : na, "09:30 anchored VWAP", color = color.new(#ff9800, 0), linewidth = 2, style = plot.style_linebr)
// The sigma bands of that VWAP - where a sigma target actually sits.
sigOn = showVwap and inSess and not na(avwapDev)
plot(sigOn ? avwap + avwapDev     : na, "VWAP +1 sigma", color = color.new(#ff9800, 45), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(sigOn ? avwap - avwapDev     : na, "VWAP -1 sigma", color = color.new(#ff9800, 45), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(sigOn ? avwap + 2 * avwapDev : na, "VWAP +2 sigma", color = color.new(#ff9800, 62), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(sigOn ? avwap - 2 * avwapDev : na, "VWAP -2 sigma", color = color.new(#ff9800, 62), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(sigOn ? avwap + 3 * avwapDev : na, "VWAP +3 sigma", color = color.new(#ff9800, 78), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(sigOn ? avwap - 3 * avwapDev : na, "VWAP -3 sigma", color = color.new(#ff9800, 78), style = plot.style_linebr)
// ORB / IB levels
plot(runORB and not na(or_rH) ? or_rH : na, "ORB High", color = color.new(color.orange, 0),  style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runORB and not na(or_rL) ? or_rL : na, "ORB Low",  color = color.new(color.orange, 45), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runIB and not na(ib_rH) ? ib_rH : na, "IB High", color = color.new(color.teal, 0),  style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runIB and not na(ib_rL) ? ib_rL : na, "IB Low",  color = color.new(color.teal, 45), style = plot.style_linebr)
// The live resting limit: the VWAP, but only over the bars where the order is actually on the book. A gap in
// these lines is a setup being held back, out of its window, or already filled.
plot(runORB and orbArm ? or_e1 : na, "ORB limit (live)", color = color.new(color.yellow, 0), linewidth = 2, style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runIB  and ibArm  ? ib_e1 : na, "IB limit (live)",  color = color.new(color.aqua, 0),   linewidth = 2, style = plot.style_linebr)
// Halyard's 15-minute range, drawn from the engine's own candles
plot(runHAL and not na(halRH) ? halRH : na, "Halyard range high", color = color.new(color.fuchsia, 0),  style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(runHAL and not na(halRL) ? halRL : na, "Halyard range low",  color = color.new(color.fuchsia, 45), style = plot.style_linebr)
// The breakout TRIANGLE marks the chart bar that closes the 15m candle which BREAKS the range.
plotshape(halShowMarker and halBrkUp, title = "Halyard: 15m close above range", style = shape.triangleup, location = location.abovebar, color = halUpCol, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(halShowMarker and halBrkDn, title = "Halyard: 15m close below range", style = shape.triangledown, location = location.belowbar, color = halDnCol, size = size.tiny)

// HALYARD DAY HIGHLIGHT. ORANGE = the Halyard day is Off. A faint GREEN / RED wash = the day is one-way, so the
// setting is readable off the chart instead of only out of the input dialog. Nothing is tinted on a two-way day.
halIsWeekday = halDow >= dayofweek.monday and halDow <= dayofweek.friday
bgcolor(not runHAL or not halIsWeekday ? na : not halDayOK ? color.new(color.orange, 95) : halMode == "Long" ? color.new(color.green, 96) : halMode == "Short" ? color.new(color.red, 96) : na, title = "Halyard day filter")
